[{:db/id 17592186179739 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2310204a-fdf5-57d1-9e96-98189fedc070"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2310204a-fdf5-57d1-9e96-98189fedc070" :question/id #uuid "2310204a-fdf5-57d1-9e96-98189fedc070" :question/math-academy-id "q-125490" :question/problem "![](images/9f/9f94742a7f37fd7f6a1c789401a2e323fec80aca584774453cba03cf69f28ade.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above, and let $C$ be the path along the segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n\nII. ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n\nIII. ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$  works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](images/f4/f4e8c62562ee1657e41bb36a21c901dc95935558641f724f934a4c58706f4a64.png)\n\n \n\nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. It's clear from the picture below that if we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](images/40/40b100dd4bc71b95f5ad99eb0cec8ed87133211bb371b22deccb851f79c695b3.png)\n\n \n\nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-53503a6a-a2ae-508c-9eef-c15dd0d61993"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-53503a6a-a2ae-508c-9eef-c15dd0d61993" :answer-field/id #uuid "53503a6a-a2ae-508c-9eef-c15dd0d61993" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7ed18d44-37e8-529c-a585-0ceab88f3f9f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d8ee07b7-d7ad-5975-9eff-46b920985b1f" "answer-dc1fa96f-fbba-519c-ac7f-2711d8804739" "answer-7ed18d44-37e8-529c-a585-0ceab88f3f9f" "answer-8858c48e-583e-5419-89c1-66b239d5970c" "answer-b2545c5c-af10-54e4-a998-61fc386ed756"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d8ee07b7-d7ad-5975-9eff-46b920985b1f" :answer/id #uuid "d8ee07b7-d7ad-5975-9eff-46b920985b1f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc1fa96f-fbba-519c-ac7f-2711d8804739" :answer/id #uuid "dc1fa96f-fbba-519c-ac7f-2711d8804739" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ed18d44-37e8-529c-a585-0ceab88f3f9f" :answer/id #uuid "7ed18d44-37e8-529c-a585-0ceab88f3f9f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8858c48e-583e-5419-89c1-66b239d5970c" :answer/id #uuid "8858c48e-583e-5419-89c1-66b239d5970c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b2545c5c-af10-54e4-a998-61fc386ed756" :answer/id #uuid "b2545c5c-af10-54e4-a998-61fc386ed756" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179742 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-17a8497e-763c-5804-a8ea-e63d106be3fe"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-17a8497e-763c-5804-a8ea-e63d106be3fe" :question/id #uuid "17a8497e-763c-5804-a8ea-e63d106be3fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-125497" :question/problem "![](images/4e/4ee9e02184efd314371a99c6242540e5e2e6effc9e21d41a86648b433b8a6938.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)$ shown above. Let $C$ be the path where the semiellipse is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n\nII. ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n\nIII. ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true while statement II is false. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](images/1d/1d91a85ccbb948e070db738373ffc5032f4e91a0ba8e04cd14e79276b0e798f8.png)\n\nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](images/a8/a8e0bffd04fb7b765d3c654f62b1958ab55a42f0d26cbc9f2b2e31f7d8e6f775.png)\n\nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-be155506-4e79-5a1a-866f-997f1cb30ccc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-be155506-4e79-5a1a-866f-997f1cb30ccc" :answer-field/id #uuid "be155506-4e79-5a1a-866f-997f1cb30ccc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0ac92f55-bdd5-5ebb-8623-7211f79f9620" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d9563607-dd70-5767-87cb-3d112f17eed5" "answer-0ac92f55-bdd5-5ebb-8623-7211f79f96