n$$\n{L}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a94df7ac-0f23-5acc-9a88-bce1ea6077bc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a94df7ac-0f23-5acc-9a88-bce1ea6077bc" :answer-field/id #uuid "a94df7ac-0f23-5acc-9a88-bce1ea6077bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9266158b-36be-5081-ada4-69f033c39993" :answer-field/choices ["answer-68202c51-a8c7-5b41-8b8e-52288fa600be" "answer-582190fc-850a-5c44-9e79-a818e78b201e" "answer-7873d209-1846-562f-a21c-77b8683916c2" "answer-9266158b-36be-5081-ada4-69f033c39993" "answer-e7bd5536-867b-57d6-9150-07d885c15b03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-68202c51-a8c7-5b41-8b8e-52288fa600be" :answer/id #uuid "68202c51-a8c7-5b41-8b8e-52288fa600be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-582190fc-850a-5c44-9e79-a818e78b201e" :answer/id #uuid "582190fc-850a-5c44-9e79-a818e78b201e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7873d209-1846-562f-a21c-77b8683916c2" :answer/id #uuid "7873d209-1846-562f-a21c-77b8683916c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9266158b-36be-5081-ada4-69f033c39993" :answer/id #uuid "9266158b-36be-5081-ada4-69f033c39993" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e7bd5536-867b-57d6-9150-07d885c15b03" :answer/id #uuid "e7bd5536-867b-57d6-9150-07d885c15b03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7effc142-a727-5443-a7a6-2e2db67c4b1f" :question/id #uuid "7effc142-a727-5443-a7a6-2e2db67c4b1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-32008" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the elementary matrix \n$S=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $S$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[S\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse is obtained on the right-hand side of our big matrix after the transformation. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{S}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3af9e33e-f08c-574c-97d5-344ef1178cc0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3af9e33e-f08c-574c-97d5-344ef1178cc0" :answer-field/id #uuid "3af9e33e-f08c-574c-97d5-344ef1178cc0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d0ae9d64-3c04-543e-9bad-0f91c19f44f2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-77d890b8-7322-5242-a284-9e74f77fee01" "answer-726b610b-966f-5fad-8937-be3c12d0601d" "answer-db2ac3cb-cacf-5f7f-8f49-0a6d597fce81" "answer-d0ae9d64-3c04-543e-9bad-0f91c19f44f2" "answer-f6d47fd4-271e-59b7-9dfb-e64e565385a2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-77d890b8-7322-5242-a284-9e74f77fee01" :answer/id #uuid "77d890b8-7322-5242-a284-9e74f77fee01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-726b610b-966f-5fad-8937-be3c12d0601d" :answer/id #uuid "726b610b-966f-5fad-8937-be3c12d0601d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-db2ac3cb-cacf-5f7f-8f49-0a6d597fce81" :answer/id #uuid "db2ac3cb-cacf-5f7f-8f49-0a6d597fce81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d0ae9d64-3c04-543e-9bad-0f91c19f44f2" :answer/id #uuid "d0ae9d64-3c04-543e-9bad-0f91c19f44f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f6d47fd4-271e-59b7-9dfb-e64e565385a2" :answer/id #uuid "f6d47fd4-271e-59b7-9dfb-e64e565385a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115245 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5238d337-5418-5670-995a-6cacdf9c34e1" "question-3433ea61-fe1b-529a-a624-2ade0d70ec66"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-5238d337-5418-5670-995a-6cacdf9c34e1" :question/id #uuid "5238d337-5418-5670-995a-6cacdf9c34e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-130816" :question/problem "Find the product ${E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{E}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that ${E}_{1}$ and ${E}_{2}$ are both elementary matrices.\n\nFirst, we need to find ${E}_{1}^{-1}.$ We write down ${E}_{1}$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[{E}_{1}\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{E}_{1}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we can find the product ${E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n{E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2aa55760-fe42-5b20-a3f8-0684f066d9d1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2aa55760-fe42-5b20-a3f8-0684f066d9d1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2aa55760-fe42-5b20-a3f8-0684f066d9d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-171d85cf-363f-5e91-8844-7377fbfe4868" :answer-field/choices ["answer-171d85cf-363f-5e91-8844-7377fbfe4868" "answer-b8d97c63-845a-5df4-bd21-ef85ce115fe4" "answer-d7b02096-c5f8-533f-a7c6-397872aa44c6" "answer-d05c1129-f39e-5113-b571-d89546b3420c" "answer-abc41fe2-4fc6-5168-adaa-26ac614241df"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-171d85cf-363f-5e91-8844-7377fbfe4868" :answer/id #uuid "171d85cf-363f-5e91-8844-7377fbfe4868" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8d97c63-845a-5df4-bd21-ef85ce115fe4" :answer/id #uuid "b8d97c63-845a-5df4-bd21-ef85ce115fe4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d7b02096-c5f8-533f-a7c6-397872aa44c6" :answer/id #uuid "d7b02096-c5f8-533f-a7c6-397872aa44c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d05c1129-f39e-5113-b571-d89546b3420c" :answer/id #uuid "d05c1129-f39e-5113-b571-d89546b3420c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-abc41fe2-4fc6-5168-adaa-26ac614241df" :answer/id #uuid "abc41fe2-4fc6-5168-adaa-26ac614241df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115841 :question/problem "Find the product ${E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{E}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that ${E}_{1}$ and ${E}_{2}$ are both elementary matrices.\n\nFirst, we need to find ${E}_{1}^{-1}.$ We write down ${E}_{1}$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[{E}_{1}\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -7 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+7{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{E}_{1}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we can find the product ${E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n{E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}15 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186113983 :answer-field/correct "answer-9f574a63-4cd5-5ba3-aee2-b3411a92aab5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a1f3902b-ad8b-5c0c-8a37-a910843374dd" "answer-3d5cf453-a524-596c-a71c-3cc10ff9251a" "answer-cb2def03-42ec-5d22-9a67-872732233e9a" "answer-d9d061de-733c-5ff8-b08f-66b5ba33a70c" "answer-9f574a63-4cd5-5ba3-aee2-b3411a92aab5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a1f3902b-ad8b-5c0c-8a37-a910843374dd" :answer/id #uuid "a1f3902b-ad8b-5c0c-8a37-a910843374dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d5cf453-a524-596c-a71c-3cc10ff9251a" :answer/id #uuid "3d5cf453-a524-596c-a71c-3cc10ff9251a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb2def03-42ec-5d22-9a67-872732233e9a" :answer/id #uuid "cb2def03-42ec-5d22-9a67-872732233e9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}15 & -7 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d9d061de-733c-5ff8-b08f-66b5ba33a70c" :answer/id #uuid "d9d061de-733c-5ff8-b08f-66b5ba33a70c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}15 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f574a63-4cd5-5ba3-aee2-b3411a92aab5" :answer/id #uuid "9f574a63-4cd5-5ba3-aee2-b3411a92aab5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}15 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3433ea61-fe1b-529a-a624-2ade0d70ec66" :question/id #uuid "3433ea61-fe1b-529a-a624-2ade0d70ec66" :question/math-academy-id "q-130818" :question/problem "Find the product ${E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{E}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that ${E}_{1}$ and ${E}_{2}$ are both elementary matrices.\n\nFirst, we need to find ${E}_{1}^{-1}.$ We write down ${E}_{1}$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[{E}_{1}\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{2}:=(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{E}_{1}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we can find the product ${E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n{E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-78d3bcbf-8ec9-56b3-920b-0ce0b0b51783"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-78d3bcbf-8ec9-56b3-920b-0ce0b0b51783" :answer-field/id #uuid "78d3bcbf-8ec9-56b3-920b-0ce0b0b51783" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-359a8301-f2b5-525c-9c59-3eca56ed7220" :answer-field/choices ["answer-359a8301-f2b5-525c-9c59-3eca56ed7220" "answer-c4801de1-59ca-57fe-b0c0-05d352233bf2" "answer-d128f841-a358-5f8c-9454-d6b460a2413f" "answer-954ac438-6aab-5e66-944b-f44c338618fb" "answer-a5bc2cfa-37ac-5ab0-91e9-e6abbac4d269"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-359a8301-f2b5-525c-9c59-3eca56ed7220" :answer/id #uuid "359a8301-f2b5-525c-9c59-3eca56ed7220" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4801de1-59ca-57fe-b0c0-05d352233bf2" :answer/id #uuid "c4801de1-59ca-57fe-b0c0-05d352233bf2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d128f841-a358-5f8c-9454-d6b460a2413f" :answer/id #uuid "d128f841-a358-5f8c-9454-d6b460a2413f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-954ac438-6aab-5e66-944b-f44c338618fb" :answer/id #uuid "954ac438-6aab-5e66-944b-f44c338618fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5bc2cfa-37ac-5ab0-91e9-e6abbac4d269" :answer/id #uuid "a5bc2cfa-37ac-5ab0-91e9-e6abbac4d269" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186116496 :tutorial/content "Each elementary matrix $E$ is invertible, and the corresponding inverse is always an elementary matrix of the same type as $E$.\nTo illustrate, let's consider the matrix \n\n![](images/01/0144b651cc6eff46265156e1491f58aacfc167da6dce571dbf4a92c9d94e7177.svg)\nTo find the inverse of $E,$ we proceed as follows:\n\n**Step 1:** Write down $\\color{blue}E$ and the identity matrix $I_2$ side-by-side, as shown below:\n![](images/fb/fbb291c4f2d7ccc79939cf9368579b07f6649709f123fb70a1383deefaec6fc1.svg)\n\n**Step 2:** Apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix. In our case, we need to apply the transformation $R_2 := R_2 + (-4)R_1.$ We apply the operation to the entire row (not only the left part):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[E\\,|\\,{I}_{2}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[{I}_{2}\\,|\\,{E}^{-1}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix $E^{-1}$ is obtained on the right-hand side of our big matrix after the transformation. Therefore,\n![](images/1e/1e71a52dda452f98fa77c01117f40d055fa0661100a0e4ffc25147d9baefc0af.svg)\n\nWe can work out the inverse of all elementary $2 \\times 2$ matrices in a similar way." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078552 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3c476ad6-03e3-57c6-ac0c-7d3e461a358b" "question-db59e458-8e99-5a95-814f-8adc8a6a9836"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-3c476ad6-03e3-57c6-ac0c-7d3e461a358b" :question/id #uuid "3c476ad6-03e3-57c6-ac0c-7d3e461a358b" :question/math-academy-id "q-122322" :question/problem "![](images/9c/9ceef67f02c022065be31de7ec1b6785d270c194aee29c4d0a20707998932134.png)\n\nGiven the triangle above, find the length of $\\overset{―}{BC}$ rounded to one decimal place." :question/worked-solution "For an angle $\\theta $ in a right triangle, the trigonometric ratios are as follows:\n\n- $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{adjacent leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{adjacent leg}}$\n\nFirst, note that we are given the length of the hypotenuse $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and wish to find the length of the leg $\\overset{―}{BC}$ adjacent to the given angle $∠B.$\n\nThe trigonometric ratio that relates the adjacent leg to the hypotenuse is *cosine*. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{\\text{adjacent leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡({38}^{∘}) & =\\frac{BC}{12} \\\\ BC & =12\\operatorname{cos}⁡({38}^{∘}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing a calculator to evaluate the trigonometric ratio, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =12\\operatorname{cos}⁡({38}^{∘}) \\\\  & =12(0.788\\,01…) \\\\  & =9.456\\,12… \\\\  & ≈9.5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1b7b0522-84f1-5956-962e-86aea240df5c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1b7b0522-84f1-5956-962e-86aea240df5c" :answer-field/id #uuid "1b7b0522-84f1-5956-962e-86aea240df5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5a69af37-0c06-5df1-aa78-ca7c1546903d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-26256598-94e5-56e9-a905-4f642b7536ae" "answer-36140525-504a-5b6d-8a94-c1d35b940038" "answer-51d7af68-0a6e-5e14-8481-2347a142bf70" "answer-5a69af37-0c06-5df1-aa78-ca7c1546903d" "answer-093e66c5-68b2-5de8-be74-d3e1b20f43d4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26256598-94e5-56e9-a905-4f642b7536ae" :answer/id #uuid "26256598-94e5-56e9-a905-4f642b7536ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-36140525-504a-5b6d-8a94-c1d35b940038" :answer/id #uuid "36140525-504a-5b6d-8a94-c1d35b940038" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-51d7af68-0a6e-5e14-8481-2347a142bf70" :answer/id #uuid "51d7af68-0a6e-5e14-8481-2347a142bf70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5a69af37-0c06-5df1-aa78-ca7c1546903d" :answer/id #uuid "5a69af37-0c06-5df1-aa78-ca7c1546903d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-093e66c5-68b2-5de8-be74-d3e1b20f43d4" :answer/id #uuid "093e66c5-68b2-5de8-be74-d3e1b20f43d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-db59e458-8e99-5a95-814f-8adc8a6a9836" :question/id #uuid "db59e458-8e99-5a95-814f-8adc8a6a9836" :question/math-academy-id "q-122353" :question/problem "![](images/77/77242f149dc99e0641e6e095d02aeeb1fffdf764ee664cfcc02e659f9d0e03b0.png)\n\nGiven the triangle above, find the length of $\\overset{―}{AC}$ rounded to one decimal place." :question/worked-solution "For an angle $\\theta $ in a right triangle, the trigonometric ratios are as follows:\n\n- $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{adjacent leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{adjacent leg}}$\n\nFirst, note that we are given the length of the adjacent leg $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and wish to find the length of the leg $\\overset{―}{AC}$ hypotenuse to the given angle $∠A.$\n\nThe trigonometric ratio that relates the adjacent leg to the hypotenuse is *cosine*. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(m∠C) & =\\frac{\\text{adjacent leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡({22}^{∘}) & =\\frac{7}{AC} \\\\ AC\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡({22}^{∘}) & =7 \\\\ AC & =\\frac{7}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡({22}^{∘})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing a calculator to evaluate the trigonometric ratio, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\frac{7}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡({22}^{∘})} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{(0.927\\,18…)} \\\\  & =7.549\\,74… \\\\  & ≈7.5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dee662f8-4fb6-5dbb-876b-c57ec504e694"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dee662f8-4fb6-5dbb-876b-c57ec504e694" :answer-field/id #uuid "dee662f8-4fb6-5dbb-876b-c57ec504e694" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a27513fc-52d7-5aae-8114-61b988f68c53" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a4475272-1254-5374-b9a5-1ae13bf40580" "answer-a27513fc-52d7-5aae-8114-61b988f68c53" "answer-b7f65878-4423-5003-bb30-a8b179c3fc21" "answer-f715c199-77ad-5e4d-b6a4-19176a3b13e6" "answer-720d9d1c-5ab9-50e9-b083-1d77e7c43301"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a4475272-1254-5374-b9a5-1ae13bf40580" :answer/id #uuid "a4475272-1254-5374-b9a5-1ae13bf40580" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a27513fc-52d7-5aae-8114-61b988f68c53" :answer/id #uuid "a27513fc-52d7-5aae-8114-61b988f68c53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b7f65878-4423-5003-bb30-a8b179c3fc21" :answer/id #uuid "b7f65878-4423-5003-bb30-a8b179c3fc21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f715c199-77ad-5e4d-b6a4-19176a3b13e6" :answer/id #uuid "f715c199-77ad-5e4d-b6a4-19176a3b13e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-720d9d1c-5ab9-50e9-b083-1d77e7c43301" :answer/id #uuid "720d9d1c-5ab9-50e9-b083-1d77e7c43301" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078725 :question/problem "A triangle $△LMN$ has $m∠L={90}^{∘},$ $m∠N={37}^{∘},$ and $LM=8.$ Find the length of $\\overset{―}{LN}$ rounded to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "For an angle $\\theta $ in a right triangle, the trigonometric ratios are as follows:\n\n- $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{adjacent leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{adjacent leg}}$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the given triangle.\n\n![](images/38/38dcba98867c158c671b35ec033fa1ec55c8cedc67466ebe981de9fbbae314e9.png)\n\nNotice that we are given the length of the leg $\\overset{―}{LM}$ opposite to the given angle $∠N$ and wish to find the length of the leg $\\overset{―}{LN}$ adjacent$∠N.$\n\nThe trigonometric ratio that relates the opposite leg to the adjacent leg is *tangent*. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠N) & =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{adjacent leg}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({37}^{∘}) & =\\frac{8}{LN} \\\\ LN\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({37}^{∘}) & =8 \\\\ LN & =\\frac{8}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡({37}^{∘})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing a calculator to evaluate the trigonometric ratio, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}LN & =\\frac{8}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡({37}^{∘})} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{(0.753\\,55…)} \\\\  & =10.616\\,35… \\\\  & ≈11,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186075226 :answer-field/correct 17592186075231 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "activity-576dc7b4-9f19-5b00-813c-ad7409e11453" :activity/id #uuid "576dc7b4-9f19-5b00-813c-ad7409e11453" :activity/title "Calculating Side Lengths of Right Triangles Using Trigonometry" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048410 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-632f2b5c-59a9-5ba2-801e-afe343c8884d" "step-1a29101a-51c6-5a17-9630-96d384c00f92" "step-8229b54b-7fdd-521b-bccb-cd2fbf390017"] :activity/first-step "step-632f2b5c-59a9-5ba2-801e-afe343c8884d" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-632f2b5c-59a9-5ba2-801e-afe343c8884d" :step/id #uuid "632f2b5c-59a9-5ba2-801e-afe343c8884d" :step/content "question-3c476ad6-03e3-57c6-ac0c-7d3e461a358b" :step/next "step-1a29101a-51c6-5a17-9630-96d384c00f92" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-1a29101a-51c6-5a17-9630-96d384c00f92" :step/id #uuid "1a29101a-51c6-5a17-9630-96d384c00f92" :step/content "question-db59e458-8e99-5a95-814f-8adc8a6a9836" :step/next "step-8229b54b-7fdd-521b-bccb-cd2fbf390017" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-8229b54b-7fdd-521b-bccb-cd2fbf390017" :step/id #uuid "8229b54b-7fdd-521b-bccb-cd2fbf390017" :step/content 17592186078725 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186316630 :answer-field/choices 17592186316403] [:db/retract 17592186316832 :answer-field/choices 17592186316280] [:db/retract 17592186316880 :answer-field/choices 17592186315550] [:db/retract 17592186316997 :answer-field/choices 17592186315151] [:db/retract 17592186316776 :answer-field/choices 17592186316223] {:db/id 17592186221449 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6acce05c-927e-54a3-ab7e-dea3332ed930" "question-e3e7079a-616c-59e7-8130-14cd0fb2782d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186221451 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ed658204-766e-56cd-a12e-1cf2b14b40f7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-6acce05c-927e-54a3-ab7e-dea3332ed930" :question/id #uuid "6acce05c-927e-54a3-ab7e-dea3332ed930" :question/math-academy-id "q-342257" :question/problem "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-5x, & x\\in [-2,0) \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}, & x\\in [0,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-2,2).$ Let $f(x)$ be the $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | ${lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-2,2).$ Its graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/64/64b557365c3642ae7a4206794080804bf2bbccb07230dfa46a4f415570f85329.png)\n\n- Statement II is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2).$ It consists of two smooth pieces.\n\n- Statement III is $\\text{true}.$ Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}-5x=-5(-2)=10\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}=\\frac{5}{2}(2)^{2}=10.\n$$\n\nSo, ${lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x).$\n\n- Statement IV is $\\text{true}$ since statements I, II, and III are all true.\n\n**Note:** The $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R$ has the graph shown below.\n\n![](images/cd/cd37979eada411b68755dfa85ec3b1e22585df2bff5c4bdd4b27cf06463706d6.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a7c63119-6c8c-562e-abc9-23fca39a632c" "answer-field-dcc6415d-3e4e-531f-9f82-1e1222466f88" "answer-field-e6e854c4-06f2-5c3a-8345-9858abe5cb7f" "answer-field-c9e2bd45-2176-5d0a-8daf-b4630614c646"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a7c63119-6c8c-562e-abc9-23fca39a632c" :answer-field/id #uuid "a7c63119-6c8c-562e-abc9-23fca39a632c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-4dc4a3af-4483-521b-bb70-d53ecf298569" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6dac34b7-0afe-57b3-92dd-0f1fe22e6081" "answer-4dc4a3af-4483-521b-bb70-d53ecf298569"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6dac34b7-0afe-57b3-92dd-0f1fe22e6081" :answer/id #uuid "6dac34b7-0afe-57b3-92dd-0f1fe22e6081" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4dc4a3af-4483-521b-bb70-d53ecf298569" :answer/id #uuid "4dc4a3af-4483-521b-bb70-d53ecf298569" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dcc6415d-3e4e-531f-9f82-1e1222466f88" :answer-field/id #uuid "dcc6415d-3e4e-531f-9f82-1e1222466f88" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-ae9e632a-9e59-5e68-bbaf-7f55bdadec72" :answer-field/choices ["answer-25e88e23-60be-52a5-b776-49ba011dac2d" "answer-ae9e632a-9e59-5e68-bbaf-7f55bdadec72"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25e88e23-60be-52a5-b776-49ba011dac2d" :answer/id #uuid "25e88e23-60be-52a5-b776-49ba011dac2d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae9e632a-9e59-5e68-bbaf-7f55bdadec72" :answer/id #uuid "ae9e632a-9e59-5e68-bbaf-7f55bdadec72" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e6e854c4-06f2-5c3a-8345-9858abe5cb7f" :answer-field/id #uuid "e6e854c4-06f2-5c3a-8345-9858abe5cb7f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-c97a6594-ee59-51ba-bb03-4d481212136d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5e730ffa-3f8d-587a-90e9-54ce2eab4291" "answer-c97a6594-ee59-51ba-bb03-4d481212136d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e730ffa-3f8d-587a-90e9-54ce2eab4291" :answer/id #uuid "5e730ffa-3f8d-587a-90e9-54ce2eab4291" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c97a6594-ee59-51ba-bb03-4d481212136d" :answer/id #uuid "c97a6594-ee59-51ba-bb03-4d481212136d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c9e2bd45-2176-5d0a-8daf-b4630614c646" :answer-field/id #uuid "c9e2bd45-2176-5d0a-8daf-b4630614c646" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-ee7734d0-53ef-5456-8980-faad9723c723" :answer-field/choices ["answer-80ea76ea-89c9-5952-ae08-cee6ace28d82" "answer-ee7734d0-53ef-5456-8980-faad9723c723"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-80ea76ea-89c9-5952-ae08-cee6ace28d82" :answer/id #uuid "80ea76ea-89c9-5952-ae08-cee6ace28d82" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee7734d0-53ef-5456-8980-faad9723c723" :answer/id #uuid "ee7734d0-53ef-5456-8980-faad9723c723" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186317256 :question/problem "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x+1, & x\\in [-2,0) \\\\ -2, & x\\in [0,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-2,2).$ Let $f(x)$ be the $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | ${lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186316630 :answer-field/correct 17592186315456 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186316832 :answer-field/correct 17592186316254 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186316880 :answer-field/correct 17592186315605 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186316997 :answer-field/correct 17592186315979 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186222026 :question/problem "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & x\\in [0,1) \\\\ x, & x\\in [-1,0)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-1,1).$ \nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-1,1)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-1,1)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | ${lim}_{x\\to -{1}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is $\\text{false}.$ The function $F(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x=0.$ Its graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/2e/2eb2120db83d33d37f1d076f7e3664a21cd1bb97ccd04aeb792cd8e510edf846.png)\n\n- Statement II is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-1,1).$ It consists of two smooth pieces.\n\n- Statement III is $\\text{false}.$ Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{1}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to -{1}^{+}}x=-1\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}1=1.\n$$\n\nSo, ${lim}_{x\\to -{1}^{+}}F(x)\\ne {lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}F(x).$\n\n- Statement IV is $\\text{false}$ since statements I and III are false.\n\n**Note:** The $2$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R$ has the graph shown below.\n\n![](images/c9/c91cf3eea948fdce9a992c77d95bc3c8bc5165ade9e6f17ae5b7e699b0a9be9d.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186220836 :answer-field/correct 17592186220838 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186220839 :answer-field/correct 17592186220841 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186220833 :answer-field/correct 17592186220834 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186220830 :answer-field/correct 17592186220831 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-e3e7079a-616c-59e7-8130-14cd0fb2782d" :question/id #uuid "e3e7079a-616c-59e7-8130-14cd0fb2782d" :question/math-academy-id "q-342492" :question/problem "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+1, & x\\in [-3,0) \\\\ {x}^{2}+1, & x\\in [0,3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-3,3).$ Let $f(x)$ be the $6$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-3,3)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-3,3)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | ${lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-3,3).$ Its graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/66/66b91f732d36469ded18df5404b3f12dddad7474168efd47ddf038835b67b831.png)\n\n- Statement II is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-3,3).$ It consists of two smooth pieces.\n\n- Statement III is $\\text{false}.$ Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}(-2x+1)=-2(-3)+1=7\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}({x}^{2}+1)=(3)^{2}+1=10.\n$$\n\nSo, ${lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)\\ne {lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x).$\n\n- Statement IV is $\\text{false}$ since statement III is false.\n\n**Note:** The $6$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R$ has the graph shown below.\n\n![](images/88/888053858d845bd47a56b953a5eb9a6f7f6b4ddffc0ecc70fa280e1a7d543f24.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-69e99acf-1398-5692-8061-029fa2a74beb" "answer-field-56723ba2-cf0d-57bb-8655-32504888775c" "answer-field-37dba421-36d3-5977-b5b1-852f9e3aa421" "answer-field-c454f910-39f4-514e-b488-5dfacc09ef1d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-69e99acf-1398-5692-8061-029fa2a74beb" :answer-field/id #uuid "69e99acf-1398-5692-8061-029fa2a74beb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-ae6c9b1a-0549-532b-b72f-ea08c4affb51" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ae29e0f7-ed28-5cbf-85ca-f73138f17f52" "answer-ae6c9b1a-0549-532b-b72f-ea08c4affb51"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae29e0f7-ed28-5cbf-85ca-f73138f17f52" :answer/id #uuid "ae29e0f7-ed28-5cbf-85ca-f73138f17f52" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae6c9b1a-0549-532b-b72f-ea08c4affb51" :answer/id #uuid "ae6c9b1a-0549-532b-b72f-ea08c4affb51" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-56723ba2-cf0d-57bb-8655-32504888775c" :answer-field/id #uuid "56723ba2-cf0d-57bb-8655-32504888775c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-c4ef0c6d-3fca-5c4f-88d3-d5d53bd3106c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2c1a0160-ca7d-5739-9abb-99203387c9b4" "answer-c4ef0c6d-3fca-5c4f-88d3-d5d53bd3106c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c1a0160-ca7d-5739-9abb-99203387c9b4" :answer/id #uuid "2c1a0160-ca7d-5739-9abb-99203387c9b4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4ef0c6d-3fca-5c4f-88d3-d5d53bd3106c" :answer/id #uuid "c4ef0c6d-3fca-5c4f-88d3-d5d53bd3106c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-37dba421-36d3-5977-b5b1-852f9e3aa421" :answer-field/id #uuid "37dba421-36d3-5977-b5b1-852f9e3aa421" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-64a4d026-4e1a-5cce-880b-42dd87fa4270" :answer-field/choices ["answer-64a4d026-4e1a-5cce-880b-42dd87fa4270" "answer-733c52bb-6afa-5bc5-95c0-a7e66333b6e0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-64a4d026-4e1a-5cce-880b-42dd87fa4270" :answer/id #uuid "64a4d026-4e1a-5cce-880b-42dd87fa4270" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-733c52bb-6afa-5bc5-95c0-a7e66333b6e0" :answer/id #uuid "733c52bb-6afa-5bc5-95c0-a7e66333b6e0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c454f910-39f4-514e-b488-5dfacc09ef1d" :answer-field/id #uuid "c454f910-39f4-514e-b488-5dfacc09ef1d" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-82fb8f4e-8153-5912-b8f4-8e162eb48f70" :answer-field/choices ["answer-82fb8f4e-8153-5912-b8f4-8e162eb48f70" "answer-5f06001d-c0a8-5110-aaab-05496df93977"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82fb8f4e-8153-5912-b8f4-8e162eb48f70" :answer/id #uuid "82fb8f4e-8153-5912-b8f4-8e162eb48f70" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f06001d-c0a8-5110-aaab-05496df93977" :answer/id #uuid "5f06001d-c0a8-5110-aaab-05496df93977" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ed658204-766e-56cd-a12e-1cf2b14b40f7" :question/id #uuid "ed658204-766e-56cd-a12e-1cf2b14b40f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-343391" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=3{x}^{2}$ defined on $[-\\pi ,\\pi ).$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of a series converging to the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of \n\n$$\nG(x)={x}^{3}={\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nfrom the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$\n\nThe Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n3{x}^{2}∼{\\pi }^{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{12(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}} \non $R,$ we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n{x}^{3}∼{\\pi }^{2}x+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-3}}\\cdot {{field-4}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an even function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=\\pi $ and we are already given the coefficients for $n\\ge 1.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\pi }^{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{12(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the function $F$ is continuous on $(-\\pi ,\\pi ).$ \nTherefore, the $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f$ is $\\text{piecewise continuous}$ on $R,$ so we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}3{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t & ∼{\\int }_{0}^{x}({\\pi }^{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{12(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nt))\\text{d}t \\\\ [{t}^{3}]_{0}^{x} & ∼[{\\pi }^{2}t]_{0}^{x}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{12(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}\\cdot [\\frac{1}{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nt)]_{0}^{x} \\\\ {x}^{3} & ∼{\\pi }^{2}x+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{12(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b47fccdc-c568-5695-8718-41b3bbde7ccf" "answer-field-69166540-ccfc-5316-bfb5-4b3fcfefdc9f" "answer-field-07ef0176-9972-561f-b028-e97ddd2d78db" "answer-field-830beb7c-054e-556c-a7b8-6c335f330299"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b47fccdc-c568-5695-8718-41b3bbde7ccf" :answer-field/id #uuid "b47fccdc-c568-5695-8718-41b3bbde7ccf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-b4c2430c-0c6a-549e-aa2b-e39d8ffb22dc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d386d763-aaac-543d-9911-63e1963b04ac" "answer-b70050b3-2831-538a-98f7-589a10e9520d" "answer-b4c2430c-0c6a-549e-aa2b-e39d8ffb22dc" "answer-b732912b-9781-517d-a1b3-41138feb28b6" "answer-44d62fec-1344-5409-9e10-19b41bcbaf7b" "answer-18700c44-863c-5283-8d80-b4ecba9f9a9b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d386d763-aaac-543d-9911-63e1963b04ac" :answer/id #uuid "d386d763-aaac-543d-9911-63e1963b04ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{nx}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b70050b3-2831-538a-98f7-589a10e9520d" :answer/id #uuid "b70050b3-2831-538a-98f7-589a10e9520d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{nx}{\\pi })" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4c2430c-0c6a-549e-aa2b-e39d8ffb22dc" :answer/id #uuid "b4c2430c-0c6a-549e-aa2b-e39d8ffb22dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b732912b-9781-517d-a1b3-41138feb28b6" :answer/id #uuid "b732912b-9781-517d-a1b3-41138feb28b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{nx}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-44d62fec-1344-5409-9e10-19b41bcbaf7b" :answer/id #uuid "44d62fec-1344-5409-9e10-19b41bcbaf7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{nx}{\\pi })" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-18700c44-863c-5283-8d80-b4ecba9f9a9b" :answer/id #uuid "18700c44-863c-5283-8d80-b4ecba9f9a9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-69166540-ccfc-5316-bfb5-4b3fcfefdc9f" :answer-field/id #uuid "69166540-ccfc-5316-bfb5-4b3fcfefdc9f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-8777b0ac-3a0e-5d31-a627-3b0c9dbebe84" :answer-field/choices ["answer-99bfd701-6515-5005-8a6e-47fa0952ac7e" "answer-c682cd8a-5047-5bd5-a8d6-6a17186d63e1" "answer-e5abb8c6-bda3-5383-a2ac-4d9524e3087c" "answer-8777b0ac-3a0e-5d31-a627-3b0c9dbebe84"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-99bfd701-6515-5005-8a6e-47fa0952ac7e" :answer/id #uuid "99bfd701-6515-5005-8a6e-47fa0952ac7e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "even" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c682cd8a-5047-5bd5-a8d6-6a17186d63e1" :answer/id #uuid "c682cd8a-5047-5bd5-a8d6-6a17186d63e1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :a