:answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-8d023eb8-c4b2-5e63-b903-0a4aad1a6e6f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-027a294e-227d-54ff-b32b-a9a0825826cf" "answer-ceb2697a-1f56-5232-817e-c893b1311b5c" "answer-9d567457-ffee-58cf-88c6-298a9e0180fb" "answer-8d023eb8-c4b2-5e63-b903-0a4aad1a6e6f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-027a294e-227d-54ff-b32b-a9a0825826cf" :answer/id #uuid "027a294e-227d-54ff-b32b-a9a0825826cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ceb2697a-1f56-5232-817e-c893b1311b5c" :answer/id #uuid "ceb2697a-1f56-5232-817e-c893b1311b5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d567457-ffee-58cf-88c6-298a9e0180fb" :answer/id #uuid "9d567457-ffee-58cf-88c6-298a9e0180fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d023eb8-c4b2-5e63-b903-0a4aad1a6e6f" :answer/id #uuid "8d023eb8-c4b2-5e63-b903-0a4aad1a6e6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186222030 :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $4$-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=8x$ defined on $[-2,2).$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of a series converging to the $4$-periodic extension of \n\n$$\nG(x)=4{x}^{2}={\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nfrom the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$\n\nThe Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n8x∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{32(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}} \non $R,$ we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-3}}\\cdot {{field-4}}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186316776 :answer-field/correct 17592186316129 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186052449 :answer-field/choices 17592186052450] [:db/retract 17592186052449 :answer-field/choices 17592186052451] [:db/retract 17592186052449 :answer-field/choices 17592186052452] [:db/retract 17592186052449 :answer-field/choices 17592186052453] [:db/retract 17592186052449 :answer-field/choices 17592186052454] {:db/id 17592186054758 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-20eb9dff-e6a3-54ea-a4e3-f227327ba30b" "question-2be8c3b4-39c9-5644-83d2-b15c8e4f70a2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-20eb9dff-e6a3-54ea-a4e3-f227327ba30b" :question/id #uuid "20eb9dff-e6a3-54ea-a4e3-f227327ba30b" :question/math-academy-id "q-111093" :question/problem "Rationalize the denominator of $\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the denominator's conjugate is $\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nNow, to rationalize the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by the conjugate $\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2},$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{3(\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2})}{(\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{2})(\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2})} & = \\\\ \\frac{3(\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2})}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}-(\\sqrt{2})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{3(\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2})}{3-2} & = \\\\ 3(\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d19fc5b9-fae1-5789-b1b0-38f6339993d6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d19fc5b9-fae1-5789-b1b0-38f6339993d6" :answer-field/id #uuid "d19fc5b9-fae1-5789-b1b0-38f6339993d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7a60e70d-bb07-5822-9f42-ff95fb91e079" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9adb5171-3077-5713-b717-2d95d30d3fea" "answer-daa51955-ac64-5d0a-9e18-fab91aef7595" "answer-7a60e70d-bb07-5822-9f42-ff95fb91e079" "answer-6bdaf800-b113-54a1-8ae2-bf3062dae2e8" "answer-faddeef1-1236-5ec3-943a-ec3424761ede"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9adb5171-3077-5713-b717-2d95d30d3fea" :answer/id #uuid "9adb5171-3077-5713-b717-2d95d30d3fea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-daa51955-ac64-5d0a-9e18-fab91aef7595" :answer/id #uuid "daa51955-ac64-5d0a-9e18-fab91aef7595" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3(\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a60e70d-bb07-5822-9f42-ff95fb91e079" :answer/id #uuid "7a60e70d-bb07-5822-9f42-ff95fb91e079" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3(\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6bdaf800-b113-54a1-8ae2-bf3062dae2e8" :answer/id #uuid "6bdaf800-b113-54a1-8ae2-bf3062dae2e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2(\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{3})}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-faddeef1-1236-5ec3-943a-ec3424761ede" :answer/id #uuid "faddeef1-1236-5ec3-943a-ec3424761ede" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3(\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2})}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186055197 :question/problem "Rationalize the denominator of $\\frac{1-\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}+1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the denominator's conjugate is $\\sqrt{3}-1.$\n\nNow, to rationalize the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by the conjugate $\\sqrt{3}+1,$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1-\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}+1} & = \\\\ \\frac{1-\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}+1}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{\\sqrt{3}-1} & = \\\\ \\frac{(1-\\sqrt{3})(\\sqrt{3}-1)}{(\\sqrt{3}+1)(\\sqrt{3}-1)} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1-(\\sqrt{3})^{2}+\\sqrt{3}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}-(1)^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1-3+\\sqrt{3}}{3-1} & = \\\\ \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}-4}{2} & = \\\\ \\frac{2(\\sqrt{3}-2)}{2} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{3}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186052449 :answer-field/correct "answer-48563d18-51b3-56ca-8174-bcd3d2395f03" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bc408780-d5be-5c9c-a818-aa55dd20d3a7" "answer-1f951e3d-f904-57c0-a208-d0aa3eba31c4" "answer-d62ec90e-b49c-5418-9264-c77f8cc9f9fb" "answer-2420e859-faac-5e9c-aad9-2c3cc3554c7d" "answer-48563d18-51b3-56ca-8174-bcd3d2395f03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bc408780-d5be-5c9c-a818-aa55dd20d3a7" :answer/id #uuid "bc408780-d5be-5c9c-a818-aa55dd20d3a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}+5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f951e3d-f904-57c0-a208-d0aa3eba31c4" :answer/id #uuid "1f951e3d-f904-57c0-a208-d0aa3eba31c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}+5}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d62ec90e-b49c-5418-9264-c77f8cc9f9fb" :answer/id #uuid "d62ec90e-b49c-5418-9264-c77f8cc9f9fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2420e859-faac-5e9c-aad9-2c3cc3554c7d" :answer/id #uuid "2420e859-faac-5e9c-aad9-2c3cc3554c7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48563d18-51b3-56ca-8174-bcd3d2395f03" :answer/id #uuid "48563d18-51b3-56ca-8174-bcd3d2395f03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2be8c3b4-39c9-5644-83d2-b15c8e4f70a2" :question/id #uuid "2be8c3b4-39c9-5644-83d2-b15c8e4f70a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-293483" :question/problem "Rationalize the denominator of $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}+\\sqrt{3}}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the denominator's conjugate is $\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3}.$\n\nNow, to rationalize the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by the conjugate $\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3},$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}+\\sqrt{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}+\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{1(\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3})}{(\\sqrt{7}+\\sqrt{3})(\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3})} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3}}{(\\sqrt{7})^{2}-(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3}}{7-3} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-32bd77f9-d91d-5125-9cb1-16e58bc996cd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-32bd77f9-d91d-5125-9cb1-16e58bc996cd" :answer-field/id #uuid "32bd77f9-d91d-5125-9cb1-16e58bc996cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8c674107-226d-5caa-ae85-db31c6af1d97" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fb1eeb55-0e8c-536a-994c-dc2b50c74be8" "answer-a67a328f-fc73-5e16-83b9-a7b74893916b" "answer-8c674107-226d-5caa-ae85-db31c6af1d97" "answer-fd397035-a545-5279-b6e8-eafddd9a06ff" "answer-18fdfa3b-ba02-571e-937c-7aa13525db34"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb1eeb55-0e8c-536a-994c-dc2b50c74be8" :answer/id #uuid "fb1eeb55-0e8c-536a-994c-dc2b50c74be8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}+\\sqrt{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a67a328f-fc73-5e16-83b9-a7b74893916b" :answer/id #uuid "a67a328f-fc73-5e16-83b9-a7b74893916b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c674107-226d-5caa-ae85-db31c6af1d97" :answer/id #uuid "8c674107-226d-5caa-ae85-db31c6af1d97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd397035-a545-5279-b6e8-eafddd9a06ff" :answer/id #uuid "fd397035-a545-5279-b6e8-eafddd9a06ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-18fdfa3b-ba02-571e-937c-7aa13525db34" :answer/id #uuid "18fdfa3b-ba02-571e-937c-7aa13525db34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-fabd4cb5-bf5a-5891-a4c9-271ff3fb6b51" :activity/id #uuid "fabd4cb5-bf5a-5891-a4c9-271ff3fb6b51" :activity/title "Rationalizing Denominators With Two Terms" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048229 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-266a5f98-fcaf-5070-a367-7190c1ac8810" "step-4f180baa-e577-5d54-8841-f960239f5fee" "step-c02ceca0-d419-51b9-a528-057d88f7a23b"] :activity/first-step "step-266a5f98-fcaf-5070-a367-7190c1ac8810" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-266a5f98-fcaf-5070-a367-7190c1ac8810" :step/id #uuid "266a5f98-fcaf-5070-a367-7190c1ac8810" :step/content "question-20eb9dff-e6a3-54ea-a4e3-f227327ba30b" :step/next "step-4f180baa-e577-5d54-8841-f960239f5fee" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-4f180baa-e577-5d54-8841-f960239f5fee" :step/id #uuid "4f180baa-e577-5d54-8841-f960239f5fee" :step/content 17592186055197 :step/next "step-c02ceca0-d419-51b9-a528-057d88f7a23b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c02ceca0-d419-51b9-a528-057d88f7a23b" :step/id #uuid "c02ceca0-d419-51b9-a528-057d88f7a23b" :step/content "question-2be8c3b4-39c9-5644-83d2-b15c8e4f70a2" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186061068 :answer-field/choices 17592186061072] [:db/retract 17592186061068 :answer-field/choices 17592186061073] [:db/retract 17592186061068 :answer-field/choices 17592186061069] [:db/retract 17592186061068 :answer-field/choices 17592186061070] [:db/retract 17592186061068 :answer-field/choices 17592186061071] {:db/id 17592186064473 :question/problem "| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.5$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ |\n\nLet ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{50}$ be a random sample of size $n=50$ from a population with the probability mass function given above. Find an approximation for the probability that the sample mean is greater than $2.2.$\n\n*Note: $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution.*" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a random sample of size $n$ from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population standard deviation $\\sigma .$ The central limit theorem (or CLT) states that for sufficiently large $n,$ the distribution of the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ can be approximated as \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{X}∼N\\,(\\mu ,\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n}).\n$$\n\nIn our case:\n\n- the sample size is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =50,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- the population mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mu  & =\\text{E}[X] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}f({x}_{i}) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.5+2\\cdot 0.2+3\\cdot 0.1+4\\cdot 0.2 \\\\  & =0.5+0.4+0.3+0.8 \\\\  & =2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- the population variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =({1}^{2}\\cdot 0.5+{2}^{2}\\cdot 0.2+{3}^{2}\\cdot 0.1+{4}^{2}\\cdot 0.2)-{2}^{2} \\\\  & =(0.5+0.8+0.9+3.2)-4 \\\\  & =1.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by the CLT, we have that the distribution of the sample mean can be approximated as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{X} & ∼N\\,(\\mu ,\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n}) \\\\  & ∼N\\,(2,\\frac{1.4}{50}) \\\\  & ∼N(2,0.028).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to find $P(\\overset{―}{X}>2.2).$ So, we convert $\\overset{―}{X}$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\overset{―}{X}>2.2) & ≈P(Z>\\frac{2.2-2}{\\sqrt{0.028}}) \\\\  & =P(Z>1.20) \\\\  & =1-Φ(1.20).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nP(\\overset{―}{X}>2.2)=1-Φ(1.20).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186061068 :answer-field/correct "answer-4390c73f-e235-5d8c-b21e-b2ce65a311eb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e3047eec-f665-516c-929d-83b012053579" "answer-57e71192-a1a2-5e8e-aef