egin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\nWhen ${c}_{2}=1,$ we get the following curve:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x={{field-6}} \\\\ y={e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates (rounded to two decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $-0.5$ | $0$ | $0.5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-0.11$ | $0$ | {{field-7}} |\n| $y$ | $0.22$ | $1$ | {{field-8}} |\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](images/ee/eed535cfbba657a10aa37ffd90c4de36ae85e5acfa6e44b1790ec3372da10c3c.png)\n\nThe phase portrait of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/4e/4eaab4510bb15a7207aedaf37bff252132f62550d5dc62373aea0b506b7b0611.png)" :question/worked-solution "Since we have a repeated eigenvalue $\\lambda =3$ (of multiplicity two) and only one corresponding eigenvector $v,$ the solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}v{e}^{\\lambda t}+{c}_{2}(vt{e}^{\\lambda t}+w{e}^{\\lambda t}\\,),\n$$\n\nwhere $w$ is a solution to the equation $(A-\\lambda I)w=v.$\n\nIn our case, \n\n$$\n\\lambda =3,\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \nThus, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}] & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}+{c}_{2}([\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]t{e}^{3t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}{e}^{3t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{3t}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{3t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $x\\text{-axis}.$ Since ${e}^{3t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions move toward $\\text{infinity}$ in the phase plane as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](images/98/98fc60d566b520f3d943e42ee8f4e07aa0bdd33b53fbb04981c2e8f4001210fd.png)\n\nNow, consider solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{3t}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\nWhen ${c}_{2}=1,$ we get the following curve:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=t{e}^{3t} \\\\ y={e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the coordinates (rounded to two decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $-0.5$ | $0$ | $0.5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-0.11$ | $0$ | $2.24$ |\n| $y$ | $0.22$ | $1$ | $4.48$ |\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](images/ee/eed535cfbba657a10aa37ffd90c4de36ae85e5acfa6e44b1790ec3372da10c3c.png)\n\nThe phase portrait of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/4e/4eaab4510bb15a7207aedaf37bff252132f62550d5dc62373aea0b506b7b0611.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-13b526db-cf02-5f36-a044-7d6b75922f0e" "answer-field-1d559e77-3221-5ec4-bfec-a6bad1a58aeb" "answer-field-c9fc5b12-87fe-5865-9e79-aed5d58812dc" "answer-field-e4527180-f754-595e-9604-e5840563a9e9" "answer-field-d18670f6-9aee-5d4e-95a6-103b067c4c13" "answer-field-6b31599a-fb7d-511d-a4f3-9609009a28da" "answer-field-786a92ce-f877-58bb-a1d2-e3363147e257" "answer-field-87b2b6b5-d612-52ef-9a8d-9668d3c16473"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-13b526db-cf02-5f36-a044-7d6b75922f0e" :answer-field/id #uuid "13b526db-cf02-5f36-a044-7d6b75922f0e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-75aa5e5b-700c-53ad-aec6-1adbaed46b85" :answer-field/choices ["answer-683fbbc1-c806-50d9-85a2-308dfd7a7a36" "answer-75aa5e5b-700c-53ad-aec6-1adbaed46b85" "answer-a76d076d-96cf-5f10-aa9f-cad8b99ef4fc" "answer-2d2b6588-f32d-5385-bd36-7b8f041a190c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-683fbbc1-c806-50d9-85a2-308dfd7a7a36" :answer/id #uuid "683fbbc1-c806-50d9-85a2-308dfd7a7a36" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t{e}^{-3t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "a