ion-31fc7ad4-02c1-5d63-bb54-860ef7ba25ac"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-31fc7ad4-02c1-5d63-bb54-860ef7ba25ac" :question/id #uuid "31fc7ad4-02c1-5d63-bb54-860ef7ba25ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-1802" :question/problem "Evaluate $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{3}).$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{3})$ means the same thing as ${}_{7}{C}_{3}.$\n\n In general, the number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{C}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=7$ and $r=3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{7}{C}_{3} & =\\frac{7!}{(7-3)!3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7!}{4!3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5\\cdot \\cancel{4!}}{\\cancel{4!}3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5}{6} \\\\  & =35.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b1a5a15e-ede3-5556-ae58-86c4c81f9d96"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b1a5a15e-ede3-5556-ae58-86c4c81f9d96" :answer-field/id #uuid "b1a5a15e-ede3-5556-ae58-86c4c81f9d96" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ddae95b6-690f-5af4-a9a8-b1a950ef1aa3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-05bc4eb8-604f-53ae-8cad-cebb805ad20d" "answer-65546efd-9ca8-5f2d-8c2c-136dd631ea88" "answer-28eaf4dc-a8b0-5796-9977-06739a824eef" "answer-ddae95b6-690f-5af4-a9a8-b1a950ef1aa3" "answer-a49f8fb6-757b-5132-94c8-92eac2ab0522"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-05bc4eb8-604f-53ae-8cad-cebb805ad20d" :answer/id #uuid "05bc4eb8-604f-53ae-8cad-cebb805ad20d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "110" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-65546efd-9ca8-5f2d-8c2c-136dd631ea88" :answer/id #uuid "65546efd-9ca8-5f2d-8c2c-136dd631ea88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "180" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-28eaf4dc-a8b0-5796-9977-06739a824eef" :answer/id #uuid "28eaf4dc-a8b0-5796-9977-06739a824eef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "210" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ddae95b6-690f-5af4-a9a8-b1a950ef1aa3" :answer/id #uuid "ddae95b6-690f-5af4-a9a8-b1a950ef1aa3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "35" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a49f8fb6-757b-5132-94c8-92eac2ab0522" :answer/id #uuid "a49f8fb6-757b-5132-94c8-92eac2ab0522" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "420" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186354383 :question/problem "Evaluate $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{25}{0}).$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{25}{0})$ means the same thing as ${}_{25}{C}_{0}.$\n\n In general, the number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{C}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=25$ and $r=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{25}{C}_{0} & =\\frac{25!}{(25-0)!0!} \\\\  & =\\frac{25!}{25!0!} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{25!}}{\\cancel{25!}\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-bb459970-a15b-5219-80ad-e6f542ce56c5" :activity/id #uuid "bb459970-a15b-5219-80ad-e6f542ce56c5" :activity/title "Combinations" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049434 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-314e0b58-65bb-533e-b437-e2dbd19da869" "step-4e72fa17-5558-5e4e-ace4-52051946e318" "step-dffa73c5-7ead-5048-bee5-5764f9977efe"] :activity/first-step "step-314e0b58-65bb-533e-b437-e2dbd19da869" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-314e0b58-65bb-533e-b437-e2dbd19da869" :step/id #uuid "314e0b58-65bb-533e-b437-e2dbd19da869" :step/content "question-31fc7ad4-02c1-5d63-bb54-860ef7ba25ac" :step/next "step-4e72fa17-5558-5e4e-ace4-52051946e318" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-4e72fa17-5558-5e4e-ace4-52051946e318" :step/id #uuid "4e72fa17-5558-5e4e-ace4-52051946e318" :step/content 17592186332935 :step/next "step-dffa73c5-7ead-5048-bee5-5764f9977efe" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-dffa73c5-7ead-5048-bee5-5764f9977efe" :step/id #uuid "dffa73c5-7ead-5048-bee5-5764f9977efe" :step/content 17592186354383 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124591 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-60c155e6-f24c-5a27-86a4-e2d2fb148ceb" "question-6c7a58a4-6c9f-528f-bd18-00fe71c43a41" "question-31d0899c-0442-5601-b2c5-58d91ebde08a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-60c155e6-f24c-5a27-86a4-e2d2fb148ceb" :question/id #uuid "60c155e6-f24c-5a27-86a4-e2d2fb148ceb" :question/math-academy-id "q-107105" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${R}_{3}[t]$ of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $3,$ and its subset $B=\\{a{t}^{3}+b{t}^{2}+ct\\,|\\,a,b,c\\in Q\\}.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $B$ is closed under polynomial addition\n\nII. $B$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\nIII. $B$ is a subspace of ${R}_{3}[t]$\n\nIV. $B$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}_{3}[t]$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If $f(t)={a}_{1}{t}^{3}+{b}_{1}{t}^{2}+{c}_{1}t$ and $g(t)={a}_{2}{t}^{3}+{b}_{2}{t}^{2}+{c}_{2}t$ are two polynomials from $B,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)+g(t) & =({a}_{1}{t}^{3}+{b}_{1}{t}^{2}+{c}_{1}t)+({a}_{2}{t}^{3}+{b}_{2}{t}^{2}+{c}_{2}t) \\\\  & =({a}_{1}+{a}_{2}){t}^{3}+({b}_{1}+{b}_{2}){t}^{2}+({c}_{1}+{c}_{2})t,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a polynomial from $B$ since ${a}_{1}+{a}_{2},\\,{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{1}+{c}_{2}$ are in $Q.$ So, $B$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, if $f(t)={t}^{2}$ and $k=\\sqrt{2},$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kf(t) & =\\sqrt{2}{t}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is not a polynomial from $B,$ because $\\sqrt{2}\\notin Q.$ So, $B$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $B$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and IV only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f070b514-e12a-594a-9f0a-12adec04946c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f070b514-e12a-594a-9f0a-12adec04946c" :answer-field/id #uuid "f070b514-e12a-594a-9f0a-12adec04946c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4612c1ea-e787-5a0f-9afd-4cb22364e736" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4612c1ea-e787-5a0f-9afd-4cb22364e736" "answer-e348dd7c-e0f2-5cdc-b689-171bce7919c3" "answer-6511a88a-c64f-5a4e-97b4-ca39d5115c6c" "answer-7e106959-31eb-50bf-a9a4-3a9026f280bf" "answer-cd0ae82c-0963-5f9f-8291-b4680c80bd19"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4612c1ea-e787-5a0f-9afd-4cb22364e736" :answer/id #uuid "4612c1ea-e787-5a0f-9afd-4cb22364e736" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e348dd7c-e0f2-5cdc-b689-171bce7919c3" :answer/id #uuid "e348dd7c-e0f2-5cdc-b689-171bce7919c3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6511a88a-c64f-5a4e-97b4-ca39d5115c6c" :answer/id #uuid "6511a88a-c64f-5a4e-97b4-ca39d5115c6c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e106959-31eb-50bf-a9a4-3a9026f280bf" :answer/id #uuid "7e106959-31eb-50bf-a9a4-3a9026f280bf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd0ae82c-0963-5f9f-8291-b4680c80bd19" :answer/id #uuid "cd0ae82c-0963-5f9f-8291-b4680c80bd19" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6c7a58a4-6c9f-528f-bd18-00fe71c43a41" :question/id #uuid "6c7a58a4-6c9f-528f-bd18-00fe71c43a41" :question/math-academy-id "q-107100" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${R}_{4}[t]$ of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $4,$ and its subset $A$ containing all polynomials of the form $a{t}^{4}+b{t}^{2},$ with $a,b\\in R.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ is closed under polynomial addition\n\nII. $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\nIII. $A$ is a subspace of ${R}_{4}[t]$\n\nIV. $A$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}_{4}[t]$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If $f(t)={a}_{1}{t}^{4}+{b}_{1}{t}^{2}$ and $g(t)={a}_{2}{t}^{4}+{b}_{2}{t}^{2}$ are two polynomials from $A,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)+g(t) & =({a}_{1}{t}^{4}+{b}_{1}{t}^{2})+({a}_{2}{t}^{4}+{b}_{2}{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =({a}_{1}+{a}_{2}){t}^{4}+({b}_{1}+{b}_{2}){t}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a polynomial from $A.$ So, $A$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $f(t)=a{t}^{4}+b{t}^{2}\\in A$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kf(t) & =k(a{t}^{4}+b{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =(ka){t}^{4}+(kb){t}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a polynomial from $A.$ So, $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true while statement IV is false. $A$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a6dae02d-3330-5599-b891-e70cc5b6da2d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a6dae02d-3330-5599-b891-e70cc5b6da2d" :answer-field/id #uuid "a6dae02d-3330-5599-b891-e70cc5b6da2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2163c318-abcd-55be-97b4-9c32ae05ee00" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6f9e122e-367c-547e-8352-7b179ded0c2c" "answer-00ec3d76-867e-58df-a0fc-17b645b9779c" "answer-2163c318-abcd-55be-97b4-9c32ae05ee00" "answer-b04219c9-c7a8-5a0f-8c99-1a0abd96a1ce" "answer-9ff1609f-3749-592a-a12b-50db0a8cc577"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6f9e122e-367c-547e-8352-7b179ded0c2c" :answer/id #uuid "6f9e122e-367c-547e-8352-7b179ded0c2c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-00ec3d76-867e-58df-a0fc-17b645b9779c" :answer/id #uuid "00ec3d76-867e-58df-a0fc-17b645b9779c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2163c318-abcd-55be-97b4-9c32ae05ee00" :answer/id #uuid "2163c318-abcd-55be-97b4-9c32ae05ee00" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b04219c9-c7a8-5a0f-8c99-1a0abd96a1ce" :answer/id #uuid "b04219c9-c7a8-5a0f-8c99-1a0abd96a1ce" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9ff1609f-3749-592a-a12b-50db0a8cc577" :answer/id #uuid "9ff1609f-3749-592a-a12b-50db0a8cc577" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-31d0899c-0442-5601-b2c5-58d91ebde08a" :question/id #uuid "31d0899c-0442-5601-b2c5-58d91ebde08a" :question/math-academy-id "q-94616" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${R}_{5}[t]$ of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $5,$ and its subset $A$ containing all polynomials of the form $a{t}^{5},$ where $a\\in R.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true? \n\nI. $A$ is closed under polynomial addition\n\nII. $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\nIII. $A$ is a subspace of ${R}_{5}[t]$\n\nIV. $A$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}_{5}[t]$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If $f(t)={a}_{1}{t}^{5}$ and $g(t)={a}_{2}{t}^{5},$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)+g(t) & ={a}_{1}{t}^{5}+{a}_{2}{t}^{5} \\\\  & =({a}_{1}+{a}_{2}){t}^{5},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a polynomial from $A.$ So, $A$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $f(t)=a{t}^{5}$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kf(t) & =ka{t}^{5} \\\\  & =(ka){t}^{5},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a polynomial from $A.$ So, $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true while statement IV is false. $A$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fc1d8442-a2da-505e-aaa8-1ed74221f3da"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fc1d8442-a2da-505e-aaa8-1ed74221f3da" :answer-field/id #uuid "fc1d8442-a2da-505e-aaa8-1ed74221f3da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8ac94541-a732-5a4d-b872-29df378de699" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ec5175b1-31a1-53ab-8237-6c7fc548fae5" "answer-df76d186-e3ec-5f89-9781-557292058054" "answer-8ac94541-a732-5a4d-b872-29df378de699" "answer-0633560a-9503-5656-8072-6bcc75a4445c" "answer-fb99258c-ef45-5fe2-b87d-9b48445cde8c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ec5175b1-31a1-53ab-8237-6c7fc548fae5" :answer/id #uuid "ec5175b1-31a1-53ab-8237-6c7fc548fae5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-df76d186-e3ec-5f89-9781-557292058054" :answer/id #uuid "df76d186-e3ec-5f89-9781-557292058054" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ac94541-a732-5a4d-b872-29df378de699" :answer/id #uuid "8ac94541-a732-5a4d-b872-29df378de699" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0633560a-9503-5656-8072-6bcc75a4445c" :answer/id #uuid "0633560a-9503-5656-8072-6bcc75a4445c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb99258c-ef45-5fe2-b87d-9b48445cde8c" :answer/id #uuid "fb99258c-ef45-5fe2-b87d-9b48445cde8c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204581 :question/problem "Consider the functions $y:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{2}$ and $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined by\n\n$$\ny(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(y)=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is \n$\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))$ evaluated at \n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))|}_{{x}_{0}}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$42$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$18$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}+{y}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}+{y}_{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}{y}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}{y}_{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ {y}_{2} & {y}_{1}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${y}_{0}=y({x}_{0})=[\\begin{aligned}1\\cdot 2\\cdot 3 \\\\ 1+2+3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{3}$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $y$ with respect to $x$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{3}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{3}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}{x}_{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}{x}_{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{3}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}{x}_{3}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{3}}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}{x}_{3} & {x}_{1}{x}_{3} & {x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x)){|}_{{x}_{0}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 42 & 24 & 18\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203420 :answer-field/correct "answer-dcc67051-2347-5c4e-9e43-c494abdd7e5e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dcc67051-2347-5c4e-9e43-c494abdd7e5e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dcc67051-2347-5c4e-9e43-c494abdd7e5e" :answer/id #uuid "dcc67051-2347-5c4e-9e43-c494abdd7e5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203419 :answer-field/correct "answer-316633d4-c832-597f-bfdd-ba8fe21eae33" :answer-field/choices ["answer-316633d4-c832-597f-bfdd-ba8fe21eae33"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-316633d4-c832-597f-bfdd-ba8fe21eae33" :answer/id #uuid "316633d4-c832-597f-bfdd-ba8fe21eae33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203422 :answer-field/correct "answer-d6616688-0122-57c7-8244-6a4ed78090eb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d6616688-0122-57c7-8244-6a4ed78090eb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d6616688-0122-57c7-8244-6a4ed78090eb" :answer/id #uuid "d6616688-0122-57c7-8244-6a4ed78090eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203421 :answer-field/correct "answer-f5702173-007e-5e88-ab6b-3cfa857c23be" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f5702173-007e-5e88-ab6b-3cfa857c23be"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f5702173-007e-5e88-ab6b-3cfa857c23be" :answer/id #uuid "f5702173-007e-5e88-ab6b-3cfa857c23be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204589 :question/problem "Consider the functions $y:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ and $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined by\n\n$$\ny(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}) \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(y)=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}{y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is \n$\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))$ evaluated at \n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))|}_{{x}_{0}}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}{y}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}{y}_{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2} & {y}_{1} \\\\ 2{y}_{1} & 2{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${y}_{0}=y({x}_{0})=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}({0}^{2}+{2}^{2}) \\\\ 0+2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $y$ with respect to $x$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2})) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2})) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x)){|}_{{x}_{0}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203456 :answer-field/correct "answer-6f15b05f-36f5-5ea3-9bed-f930f886c722" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6f15b05f-36f5-5ea3-9bed-f930f886c722"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6f15b05f-36f5-5ea3-9bed-f930f886c722" :answer/id #uuid "6f15b05f-36f5-5ea3-9bed-f930f886c722" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203454 :answer-field/correct "answer-ec5a3336-3253-558e-8eea-a50f43e5289c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ec5a3336-3253-558e-8eea-a50f43e5289c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ec5a3336-3253-558e-8eea-a50f43e5289c" :answer/id #uuid "ec5a3336-3253-558e-8eea-a50f43e5289c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203455 :answer-field/correct "answer-a6a5ce82-7ccb-54b4-abfb-a30641f2c77e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a6a5ce82-7ccb-54b4-abfb-a30641f2c77e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6a5ce82-7ccb-54b4-abfb-a30641f2c77e" :answer/id #uuid "a6a5ce82-7ccb-54b4-abfb-a30641f2c77e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204100 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9684ce08-aa53-5b58-9612-0d1c154cab40" "question-8583a74c-8e9b-50f5-aea2-c01f0aa03b2a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9684ce08-aa53-5b58-9612-0d1c154cab40" :question/id #uuid "9684ce08-aa53-5b58-9612-0d1c154cab40" :question/math-academy-id "q-269802" :question/problem "Consider the functions $y(x)=Ax$ and $f(y)=By,$ where $x\\in {R}^{3},y\\in {R}^{2},$ and the matrices $A$ and $B$ are given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))$ evaluated at ${x}_{0}=[1,\\,-1,\\,3]^{T}?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))|}_{{x}_{0}}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-7$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ by multiplying it by $B$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}=B.\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{3}$ by multiplying it by $A$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x)) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =BA \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 6 \\\\ -7 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-91938b79-0782-57b7-a58c-c38b652b5f24" "answer-field-b6a101ae-6c02-52e5-9871-130a767d9a46" "answer-field-ff075b7b-7ca8-5b8f-88a3-0b6d0e198ed4" "answer-field-0d008ce6-0db4-5560-8335-4e57b2ea4c0d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-91938b79-0782-57b7-a58c-c38b652b5f24" :answer-field/id #uuid "91938b79-0782-57b7-a58c-c38b652b5f24" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-eb2b7682-cd57-5046-9330-476f79bd0afb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-eb2b7682-cd57-5046-9330-476f79bd0afb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb2b7682-cd57-5046-9330-476f79bd0afb" :answer/id #uuid "eb2b7682-cd57-5046-9330-476f79bd0afb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b6a101ae-6c02-52e5-9871-130a767d9a46" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6a101ae-6c02-52e5-9871-130a767d9a46" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d12784d6-1d33-593b-ad17-021cbcd94188" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d12784d6-1d33-593b-ad17-021cbcd94188"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d12784d6-1d33-593b-ad17-021cbcd94188" :answer/id #uuid "d12784d6-1d33-593b-ad17-021cbcd94188" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ff075b7b-7ca8-5b8f-88a3-0b6d0e198ed4" :answer-field/id #uuid "ff075b7b-7ca8-5b8f-88a3-0b6d0e198ed4" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-15b1b88d-fa4a-5ce4-858f-cbf3ca4ba87e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-15b1b88d-fa4a-5ce4-858f-cbf3ca4ba87e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15b1b88d-fa4a-5ce4-858f-cbf3ca4ba87e" :answer/id #uuid "15b1b88d-fa4a-5ce4-858f-cbf3ca4ba87e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0d008ce6-0db4-5560-8335-4e57b2ea4c0d" :answer-field/id #uuid "0d008ce6-0db4-5560-8335-4e57b2ea4c0d" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d9e31081-73fb-57ae-a678-67ffc4cb37a7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d9e31081-73fb-57ae-a678-67ffc4cb37a7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d9e31081-73fb-57ae-a678-67ffc4cb37a7" :answer/id #uuid "d9e31081-73fb-57ae-a678-67ffc4cb37a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8583a74c-8e9b-50f5-aea2-c01f0aa03b2a" :question/id #uuid "8583a74c-8e9b-50f5-aea2-c01f0aa03b2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-269803" :question/problem "Consider the functions $y(x)=Ax$ and $f(y)=By,$ where $x\\in {R}^{3},y\\in {R}^{2},$ and the matrices $A$ and $B$ are given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))$ evaluated at ${x}_{0}=[2,\\,-1,\\,1]^{T}?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))|}_{{x}_{0}}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">$6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-3}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ by multiplying it by $B$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}=B.\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{3}$ by multiplying it by $A$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x)) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =BA \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-726def4a-0906-5fa9-9043-394665a07fc7" "answer-field-fe571652-a4d2-5aca-a284-5cc14e649fc0" "answer-field-bd92e62f-367e-5106-b7b7-0a4661d602b0" "answer-field-183c83b2-fe77-525b-a49f-d3a9ba2e786a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-726def4a-0906-5fa9-9043-394665a07fc7" :answer-field/id #uuid "726def4a-0906-5