 :answer/id #uuid "09b99397-4784-52a1-bc2e-c34d594af14b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204101 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ed9f515f-42d2-575d-bafa-bcd19e12a760"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ed9f515f-42d2-575d-bafa-bcd19e12a760" :question/id #uuid "ed9f515f-42d2-575d-bafa-bcd19e12a760" :question/math-academy-id "q-269823" :question/problem "For $x,y,z\\in {R}^{2},$ consider the following functions: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & y(x)=Ax\\,\\text{where}\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & z(y)=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{2}-{y}_{1}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & f(z)=Cz\\,\\text{where}\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat is $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(z(y(x)))$ evaluated at ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(z(y(x)))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}z}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $z\\in {R}^{2}$ by multiplying it by $C$ and outputs a vector $f(z)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}z}=C.\n$$\n\n- The function $z$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $z(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}y}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{z}_{1}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{z}_{1}}{∂{y}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{z}_{2}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{z}_{2}}{∂{y}_{2}}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2{y}_{1} & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${y}_{0}=A{x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}2(-1) & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{2}$ by multiplying it by $A$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(z(y(x))){|}_{{x}_{0}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}z}{|}_{{z}_{0}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-34d7e51d-85f2-564b-a3f7-2300578f216d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-34d7e51d-85f2-564b-a3f7-2300578f216d" :answer-field/id #uuid "34d7e51d-85f2-564b-a3f7-2300578f216d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-80264191-38a9-5a0e-9ad8-7978f8daa096" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7e1a2103-5199-5776-8be3-a4b90b89af36" "answer-80264191-38a9-5a0e-9ad8-7978f8daa096" "answer-22bf0f43-71c0-5fe6-8a9c-db88987e135d" "answer-88597b94-66f0-5510-9176-e7d043bbb584" "answer-b3d925c6-ea55-56ff-b092-6a1d99103f84"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e1a2103-5199-5776-8be3-a4b90b89af36" :answer/id #uuid "7e1a2103-5199-5776-8be3-a4b90b89af36" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-80264191-38a9-5a0e-9ad8-7978f8daa096" :answer/id #uuid "80264191-38a9-5a0e-9ad8-7978f8daa096" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-22bf0f43-71c0-5fe6-8a9c-db88987e135d" :answer/id #uuid "22bf0f43-71c0-5fe6-8a9c-db88987e135d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-88597b94-66f0-5510-9176-e7d043bbb584" :answer/id #uuid "88597b94-66f0-5510-9176-e7d043bbb584" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b3d925c6-ea55-56ff-b092-6a1d99103f84" :answer/id #uuid "b3d925c6-ea55-56ff-b092-6a1d99103f84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-e93dbd98-aef9-5df9-aea8-c85d4eb5eb85" :activity/id #uuid "e93dbd98-aef9-5df9-aea8-c85d4eb5eb85" :activity/title "The Chain Rule for Total Derivatives" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048367 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-aeffc49e-02fd-5851-a96c-59f1d28fc3f8" "step-b0e4ff39-21d5-5469-8555-eb4203698626" "step-01c39290-cd5a-5aa1-8a59-9cbfefffe951" "step-99a98175-6d17-5897-8ff6-309efa769d68" "step-6ceaa452-9af3-59b8-a7ac-18a86e3a74a0"] :activity/first-step "step-aeffc49e-02fd-5851-a96c-59f1d28fc3f8" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-aeffc49e-02fd-5851-a96c-59f1d28fc3f8" :step/id #uuid "aeffc49e-02fd-5851-a96c-59f1d28fc3f8" :step/content 17592186204581 :step/next "step-b0e4ff39-21d5-5469-8555-eb4203698626" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-b0e4ff39-21d5-5469-8555-eb4203698626" :step/id #uuid "b0e4ff39-21d5-5469-8555-eb4203698626" :step/content 17592186204589 :step/next "step-01c39290-cd5a-5aa1-8a59-9cbfefffe951" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-01c39290-cd5a-5aa1-8a59-9cbfefffe951" :step/id #uuid "01c39290-cd5a-5aa1-8a59-9cbfefffe951" :step/content "question-9684ce08-aa53-5b58-9612-0d1c154cab40" :step/next "step-99a98175-6d17-5897-8ff6-309efa769d68" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-99a98175-6d17-5897-8ff6-309efa769d68" :step/id #uuid "99a98175-6d17-5897-8ff6-309efa769d68" :step/content "question-8583a74c-8e9b-50f5-aea2-c01f0aa03b2a" :step/next "step-6ceaa452-9af3-59b8-a7ac-18a86e3a74a0" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-6ceaa452-9af3-59b8-a7ac-18a86e3a74a0" :step/id #uuid "6ceaa452-9af3-59b8-a7ac-18a86e3a74a0" :step/content "question-ed9f515f-42d2-575d-bafa-bcd19e12a760" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129117 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fe67be82-4bb6-56a3-b9ff-5fcade759364"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129120 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fd8cef0f-9754-53fc-971e-657a61c10786" "question-47e4cafc-245d-597a-859f-2f903cb45c89"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129118 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8611bb27-3bf5-5d1d-beee-a73906924e0e" "question-a28bf299-6ff2-586b-9620-39977848687b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-fe67be82-4bb6-56a3-b9ff-5fcade759364" :question/id #uuid "fe67be82-4bb6-56a3-b9ff-5fcade759364" :question/math-academy-id "q-105592" :question/problem "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & 2x+3\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{4{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+2x+14\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,4{x}^{2}+2x+14 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\boxed{}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,8x+14 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{8x+12}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2{x}^{2}-2x+4 \\\\  & 2x+3\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{4{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+2x+14\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,4{x}^{2}+2x+14 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,4{x}^{2}-6x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,8x+14 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{8x+12}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are \n\n$\\,$ $2{x}^{2}-2x+4\\,$ and $\\,-4{x}^{2}-6x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-02161cfd-7963-5f8c-adc3-9f265f53ee14"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-02161cfd-7963-5f8c-adc3-9f265f53ee14" :answer-field/id #uuid "02161cfd-7963-5f8c-adc3-9f265f53ee14" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d37d0d7e-ef5b-5171-8f03-493fc100b9f0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c6aa7498-c71d-56f0-81d7-3d56a57c52aa" "answer-fbdd4a01-2551-59e8-a6f4-485a3a62c6c3" "answer-a342682d-0b5e-57ab-a9de-6e55658f0cb1" "answer-d37d0d7e-ef5b-5171-8f03-493fc100b9f0" "answer-0bd97d62-c94c-52ff-9437-f46824a437a6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6aa7498-c71d-56f0-81d7-3d56a57c52aa" :answer/id #uuid "c6aa7498-c71d-56f0-81d7-3d56a57c52aa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2{x}^{2}+2x+4\\,$ and $\\,4{x}^{2}-6x$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fbdd4a01-2551-59e8-a6f4-485a3a62c6c3" :answer/id #uuid "fbdd4a01-2551-59e8-a6f4-485a3a62c6c3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2{x}^{2}+x-2\\,$ and $\\,2{x}^{2}-6x$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a342682d-0b5e-57ab-a9de-6e55658f0cb1" :answer/id #uuid "a342682d-0b5e-57ab-a9de-6e55658f0cb1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2{x}^{2}-2x+4\\,$ and $\\,-2{x}^{2}-6x$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d37d0d7e-ef5b-5171-8f03-493fc100b9f0" :answer/id #uuid "d37d0d7e-ef5b-5171-8f03-493fc100b9f0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2{x}^{2}-2x+4\\,$ and $\\,-4{x}^{2}-6x$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0bd97d62-c94c-52ff-9437-f46824a437a6" :answer/id #uuid "0bd97d62-c94c-52ff-9437-f46824a437a6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2{x}^{2}-2x-2\\,$ and $\\,-2{x}^{2}-6x$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fd8cef0f-9754-53fc-971e-657a61c10786" :question/id #uuid "fd8cef0f-9754-53fc-971e-657a61c10786" :question/math-academy-id "q-37755" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomial division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6{x}^{2}-13x-5 \\\\  & -x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{-6{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}-21x+10\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-6{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,13{x}^{2}-21x+10 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{13{x}^{2}-26x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5x+10 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{5x-10}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, $\\frac{-6{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}-21x+10}{-x+2}=$" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6{x}^{2}-13x-5 \\\\  & -x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-6{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}-21x+10\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-6{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,13{x}^{2}-21x+10 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{13{x}^{2}-26x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5x+10 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{5x-10}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial $-6{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}-21x+10$ by the linear binomial $-x+2$ gives\n\n- the quotient $6{x}^{2}-13x-5,$ and\n\n- the remainder $20.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{-6{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}-21x+10}{-x+2}=6{x}^{2}-13x-5+\\frac{20}{-x+2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8ba98643-df5a-5c60-a5a0-3f92f01fcd2f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8ba98643-df5a-5c60-a5a0-3f92f01fcd2f" :answer-field/id #uuid "8ba98643-df5a-5c60-a5a0-3f92f01fcd2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6e2bb91a-2c7f-5f78-b258-108514488718" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d2fad9ad-bc30-5420-a9c9-bc1e8dc40279" "answer-3cc6f7b6-8de8-58ea-beb7-3cbd3d284763" "answer-237e2d45-91c4-5f95-88a4-a2f1d04dfafc" "answer-6e2bb91a-2c7f-5f78-b258-108514488718" "answer-ca80d411-64cf-5d0d-b7d6-d10af63a7044"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d2fad9ad-bc30-5420-a9c9-bc1e8dc40279" :answer/id #uuid "d2fad9ad-bc30-5420-a9c9-bc1e8dc40279" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6{x}^{2}-13x+5+\\frac{20}{-x+2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3cc6f7b6-8de8-58ea-beb7-3cbd3d284763" :answer/id #uuid "3cc6f7b6-8de8-58ea-beb7-3cbd3d284763" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6{x}^{2}-13x+5-\\frac{20}{-x+2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-237e2d45-91c4-5f95-88a4-a2f1d04dfafc" :answer/id #uuid "237e2d45-91c4-5f95-88a4-a2f1d04dfafc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6{x}^{2}-13x-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e2bb91a-2c7f-5f78-b258-108514488718" :answer/id #uuid "6e2bb91a-2c7f-5f78-b258-108514488718" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6{x}^{2}-13x-5+\\frac{20}{-x+2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ca80d411-64cf-5d0d-b7d6-d10af63a7044" :answer/id #uuid "ca80d411-64cf-5d0d-b7d6-d10af63a7044" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6{x}^{2}-13x-5-\\frac{20}{-x+2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-47e4cafc-245d-597a-859f-2f903cb45c89" :question/id #uuid "47e4cafc-245d-597a-859f-2f903cb45c89" :question/math-academy-id "q-38072" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomial division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}+4x+3 \\\\  & x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+11x+11\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4{x}^{2}+11x+11 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{2}+8x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3x+11 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3x+6}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, $\\frac{{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+11x+11}{x+2}=$" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}+4x+3 \\\\  & x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+11x+11\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4{x}^{2}+11x+11 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{2}+8x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3x+11 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3x+6}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial ${x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+11x+11$ by the linear binomial $x+2$ gives\n\n- the quotient ${x}^{2}+4x+3,$ and\n\n- the remainder $5.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+11x+11}{x+2}={x}^{2}+4x+3+\\frac{5}{x+2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-483aa0e1-ed0c-5589-8120-5205c6a8e4c5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-483aa0e1-ed0c-5589-8120-5205c6a8e4c5" :answer-field/id #uuid "483aa0e1-ed0c-5589-8120-5205c6a8e4c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d133fb0d-db9f-5950-9d35-052a7275add0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6830041c-00d3-5d48-9372-4d91139f97be" "answer-b62feedb-db0f-52e1-8d3c-c9470e9b162f" "answer-a3daa18e-f8f9-56bc-98a8-790e2c46a9ab" "answer-d133fb0d-db9f-5950-9d35-052a7275add0" "answer-97cc9ca4-a5bf-5661-9880-56ef534212ad"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6830041c-00d3-5d48-9372-4d91139f97be" :answer/id #uuid "6830041c-00d3-5d48-9372-4d91139f97be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4x+2+\\frac{5}{x+2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b62feedb-db0f-52e1-8d3c-c9470e9b162f" :answer/id #uuid "b62feedb-db0f-52e1-8d3c-c9470e9b162f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4x+3+\\frac{17}{x+2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3daa18e-f8f9-56bc-98a8-790e2c46a9ab" :answer/id #uuid "a3daa18e-f8f9-56bc-98a8-790e2c46a9ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4x+3+\\frac{2}{x+2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d133fb0d-db9f-5950-9d35-052a7275add0" :answer/id #uuid "d133fb0d-db9f-5950-9d35-052a7275add0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4x+3+\\frac{5}{x+2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-97cc9ca4-a5bf-5661-9880-56ef534212ad" :answer/id #uuid "97cc9ca4-a5bf-5661-9880-56ef534212ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4x+3-\\frac{5}{x+2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8611bb27-3bf5-5d1d-beee-a73906924e0e" :question/id #uuid "8611bb27-3bf5-5d1d-beee-a73906924e0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-37988" :question/problem "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & x-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{2}+0x-1} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{2}-6x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6x-1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\boxed{}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x$-term. So, we write it using a zero coefficient, as follows:\n\n$$\n6{x}^{2}+0x-1\n$$\n\nUsing the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6x+6 \\\\  & x-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{2}+0x-1} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{2}-6x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6x-1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6x-6}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are\n\n$\\,$ $6x+6\\,$ and $\\,6x-6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-31d78917-a444-511b-96e8-e5c516c9420d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-31d78917-a444-511b-96e8-e5c516c9420d" :answer-field/id #uuid "31d78917-a444-511b-96e8-e5c516c9420d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-663209ff-7566-5af2-9a93-2c990afa622e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-25c50f45-f213-5891-aa1b-f1cec1b70c2f" "answer-bd5e4bc8-abdd-5038-a814-a6f6cd9f14dc" "answer-0d703983-3af1-569b-a566-2c0828d6c6e6" "answer-663209ff-7566-5af2-9a93-2c990afa622e" "answer-0540677d-be4a-51e1-94f9-d3e8ea71916d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25c50f45-f213-5891-aa1b-f1cec1b70c2f" :answer/id #uuid "25c50f45-f213-5891-aa1b-f1cec1b70c2f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2x-6\\,$ and $\\,2x+6$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd5e4bc8-abdd-5038-a814-a6f6cd9f14dc" :answer/id #uuid "bd5e4bc8-abdd-5038-a814-a6f6cd9f14dc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$6x+1\\,$ and $\\,6x-1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d703983-3af1-569b-a566-2c0828d6c6e6" :answer/id #uuid "0d703983-3af1-569b-a566-2c0828d6c6e6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$6x+2\\,$ and $\\,6x-2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-663209ff-7566-5af2-9a93-2c990afa622e" :answer/id #uuid "663209ff-7566-5af2-9a93-2c990afa622e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$6x+6\\,$ and $\\,6x-6$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0540677d-be4a-51e1-94f9-d3e8ea71916d" :answer/id #uuid "0540677d-be4a-51e1-94f9-d3e8ea71916d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$6x-6\\,$ and $\\,6x+6$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a28bf299-6ff2-586b-9620-39977848687b" :question/id #uuid "a28bf299-6ff2-586b-9620-39977848687b" :question/math-academy-id "q-37964" :question/problem "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{2}+0x-9} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{2}+2x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-2x-9 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\boxed{}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x$-term. So, we write it using a zero coefficient, as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+0x-9\n$$\n\nUsing the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x-2 \\\\  & x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{2}+0x-9} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{2}+2x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-2x-9 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,2x-4}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are\n\n$\\,$ $x-2\\,$ and $\\,-2x-4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5193cf16-df21-588b-a599-9cd38ca21c4b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5193cf16-df21-588b-a599-9cd38ca21c4b" :answer-field/id #uuid "5193cf16-df21-588b-a599-9cd38ca21c4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f37a4a83-f662-5865-b736-284f5ac28587" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ef65b598-8ec9-5519-a1ab-5ea0b0d5f310" "answer-b24a463d-9be5-5bb5-bc05-5817742224c6" "answer-653168b4-614d-53c8-82ca-963c2033dbaf" "answer-f37a4a83-f662-5865-b736-284f5ac28587" "answer-830561b4-b28f-5d95-959b-58095c2da23b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef65b598-8ec9-5519-a1ab-5ea0b0d5f310" :answer/id #uuid "ef65b598-8ec9-5519-a1ab-5ea0b0d5f310" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2x-1\\,$ and $\\,-4x-1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b24a463d-9be5-5bb5-bc05-5817742224c6" :answer/id #uuid "b24a463d-9be5-5bb5-bc05-5817742224c6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3x-2\\,$ and $\\,2x-4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-653168b4-614d-53c8-82ca-963c2033dbaf" :answer/id #uuid "653168b4-614d-53c8-82ca-963c2033dbaf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x+2\\,$ and $\\,-2x+4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f37a4a83-f662-5865-b736-284f5ac28587" :answer/id #uuid "f37a4a83-f662-5865-b736-284f5ac28587" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x-2\\,$ and $\\,-2x-4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-830561b4-b28f-5d95-959b-58095c2da23b" :answer/id #uuid "830561b4-b28f-5d95-959b-58095c2da23b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x-2\\,$ and $\\,2x+4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064153 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4fdd627b-10f3-56fb-8e8b-56c0cb38ac41"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064272 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-99da720f-6132-59c4-9760-cafcb4cb789a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-99da720f-6132-59c4-9760-cafcb4cb789a" :question/id #uuid "99da720f-6132-59c4-9760-cafcb4cb789a" :question/math-academy-id "q-72106" :question/problem "Joseph is measuring the weight gain of his pet puppy by recording the following two numbers for different values of $t,$ where $t$ is the time, in days, since he started his observations:\n\n- $W(t)$ - The puppy's weight, in kilograms\n\n- $r(t)$ - the rate at which the puppy's weight is increasing.\n\nWhat is the relationship between $W(t)$ and $r(t)?$" :question/worked-solution "The function $W(t)$ gives the weight of the puppy after $t$ days. Then,\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}W(t)}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }W}{\\text{Change in }t}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${W}^{′}(t)$ gives the rate at which the weight of the puppy increases at time $t$, which is the same as $r(t).$ Therefore, the relationship between $W(t)$ and $r(t)$ is ${W}^{′}(t)=r(t).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cc125dcb-0e32-5fe9-99db-6daa9af7ad33"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cc125dcb-0e32-5fe9-99db-6daa9af7ad33" :answer-field/id #uuid "cc125dcb-0e32-5fe9-99db-6daa9af7ad33" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1b410e34-af3e-5a01-933c-fbe6349f45e1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9b37480b-e617-5540-824f-b3833f4eb298" "answer-7481abc5-b42c-5b1f-8b53-c6646dad9e85" "answer-a85f2065-b5b6-5ad1-8dd5-e1cb912ecdde" "answer-33d00ba0-1a85-58f1-8992-73d818d55ac7" "answer-1b410e34-af3e-5a01-933c-fbe6349f45e1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9b37480b-e617-5540-824f-b3833f4eb298" :answer/id #uuid "9b37480b-e617-5540-824f-b3833f4eb298" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "W(t)=\\frac{1}{{r}^{′}(t)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7481abc5-b42c-5b1f-8b53-c6646dad9e85" :answer/id #uuid "7481abc5-b42c-5b1f-8b53-c6646dad9e85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "W(t)=r(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a85f2065-b5b6-5ad1-8dd5-e1cb912ecdde" :answer/id #uuid "a85f2065-b5b6-5ad1-8dd5-e1cb912ecdde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "W(t)={r}^{′}(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-33d00ba0-1a85-58f1-8992-73d818d55ac7" :answer/id #uuid "33d00ba0-1a85-58f1-8992-73d818d55ac7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{W}^{′}(t)=\\frac{1}{r(t)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1b410e34-af3e-5a01-933c-fbe6349f45e1" :answer/id #uuid "1b410e34-af3e-5a01-933c-fbe6349f45e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{W}^{′}(t)=r(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4fdd627b-10f3-56fb-8e8b-56c0cb38ac41" :question/id #uuid "4fdd627b-10f3-56fb-8e8b-56c0cb38ac41" :question/math-academy-id "q-112093" :question/problem "In a factory, the cost of producing an item depends on the number of items produced per day. The function $U(x)$ models the cost, in dollars, to produce an item if the factory is producing $x$ items per day. What is the best interpretation of ${U}^{′}(500)=0.01?$" :question/worked-solution "The function ${U}^{′}(x)$ represents the rate at which the cost changes when the factory produces $x$ items per day. \n\nTherefore, ${U}^{′}(500)=0.01$ means:\n\n$\\,$ *When the factory produces $500$ items per day, the cost per item increases at a rate of $0.01$ dollars per item*" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-43e5e2b2-a362-5eae-bdb3-072556508ad1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-43e5e2b2-a362-5eae-bdb3-072556508ad1" :answer-field/id #uuid "43e5e2b2-a362-5eae-bdb3-072556508ad1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a0a04c05-0651-5009-91b0-6e14c1c0f1fb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5f045299-9859-5bcd-9090-37b7c1825618" "answer-238c54f7-d986-578c-91b7-ed7dde682958" "answer-a0a04c05-0651-5009-91b0-6e14c1c0f1fb" "answer-61078945-1d60-5c18-b427-796b3050ba43" "answer-5e540d2c-3631-53f7-a48c-010c116aa1a3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f045299-9859-5bcd-9090-37b7c1825618" :answer/id #uuid "5f045299-9859-5bcd-9090-37b7c1825618" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "For every $500$ items produced, the cost per item increases by $0.01$ dollars" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-238c54f7-d986-578c-91b7-ed7dde682958" :answer/id #uuid "238c54f7-d986-578c-91b7-ed7dde682958" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "For the first $500$ items produced, the cost per item constantly increased at a rate of $0.01$ dollars per item" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a0a04c05-0651-5009-91b0-6e14c1c0f1fb" :answer/id #uuid "a0a04c05-0651-5009-91b0-6e14c1c0f1fb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "When the factory produces $500$ items per day, the cost per item increases at a rate of $0.01$ dollars per item" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61078945-1d60-5c18-b427-796b3050ba43" :answer/id #uuid "61078945-1d60-5c18-b427-796b3050ba43" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "When the factory produces $500$ items per day, the cost per item is $0.01$ dollars" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e540d2c-3631-53f7-a48c-010c116aa1a3" :answer/id #uuid "5e540d2c-3631-53f7-a48c-010c116aa1a3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "When the factory produces $500$ items per day, the cost per item is $5$ dollars" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-57956ceb-a050-5fd1-9c8a-9b26480f8fc1" :activity/id #uuid "57956ceb-a050-5fd1-9c8a-9b26480f8fc1" :activity/title "Interpreting the Meaning of the Derivative in Context" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048835 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-a7ac6ece-a433-5e83-bad9-de6b76cd1d2a" "step-07f8cfdb-1228-53ea-a11d-e93a63c8a9d5" "step-833fadcd-bbd6-5042-880a-037df6a6b074"] :activity/first-step "step-a7ac6ece-a433-5e83-bad9-de6b76cd1d2a" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-a7ac6ece-a433-5e83-bad9-de6b76cd1d2a" :step/id #uuid "a7ac6ece-a433-5e83-bad9-de6b76cd1d2a" :step/content 17592186329911 :step/next "step-07f8cfdb-1228-53ea-a11d-e93a63c8a9d5" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-07f8cfdb-1228-53ea-a11d-e93a63c8a9d5" :step/id #uuid "07f8cfdb-1228-53ea-a11d-e93a63c8a9d5" :step/content "question-99da720f-6132-59c4-9760-cafcb4cb789a" :step/next "step-833fadcd-bbd6-5042-880a-037df6a6b074" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-833fadcd-bbd6-5042-880a-037df6a6b074" :step/id #uuid "833fadcd-bbd6-5042-880a-037df6a6b074" :step/content "question-4fdd627b-10f3-56fb-8e8b-56c0cb38ac41" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083203 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8ccbfa58-d595-551b-aac0-8c85b253cfbe" "question-84195c6c-e13d-58c7-8f62-b8364f00b637"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8ccbfa58-d595-551b-aac0-8c85b253cfbe" :question/id #uuid "8ccbfa58-d595-551b-aac0-8c85b253cfbe" :question/math-academy-id "q-18548" :question/problem "$\\frac{4{x}^{4}+12{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+16x+7}{x+3}=$" :question/worked-solution "We can calculate $\\frac{4{x}^{4}+12{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+16x+7}{x+3}$ using synthetic division.\n\nCarrying out the synthetic division process, we arrive at the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{4} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ -3 & 4 & 12 & 5 & 16 & 7 \\\\  & ↓ & -12 & 0 & -15 & -3 \\\\  & 4 & 0 & 5 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4{x}^{4}+12{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+16x+7}{x+3}=4{x}^{3}+5x+1+\\frac{4}{x+3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-711a21ce-a7d7-5796-93ec-6bc218a77acc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-711a21ce-a7d7-5796-93ec-6bc218a77acc" :answer-field/id #uuid "711a21ce-a7d7-5796-93ec-6bc218a77acc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8260834a-79a3-569a-85ef-7bdd27d16f5e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b6ca52e5-4fd3-53ba-8842-120a1f358cc2" "answer-1d1d54fd-b5da-555c-97be-008df659bd4c" "answer-8260834a-79a3-569a-85ef-7bdd27d16f5e" "answer-96603170-09ef-5253-abcf-4c72c537b471" "answer-169f6f65-5871-519b-a5b5-58af3670b1d5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b6ca52e5-4fd3-53ba-8842-120a1f358cc2" :answer/id #uuid "b6ca52e5-4fd3-53ba-8842-120a1f358cc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}^{3}+10x+11-\\frac{4}{x+3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d1d54fd-b5da-555c-97be-008df659bd4c" :answer/id #uuid "1d1d54fd-b5da-555c-97be-008df659bd4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}^{3}+2x-12+\\frac{4}{x+3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8260834a-79a3-569a-85ef-7bdd27d16f5e" :answer/id #uuid "8260834a-79a3-569a-85ef-7bdd27d16f5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}^{3}+5x+1+\\frac{4}{x+3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-96603170-09ef-5253-abcf-4c72c537b471" :answer/id #uuid "96603170-09ef-5253-abcf-4c72c537b471" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}^{3}+9x-1+\\frac{4}{x+3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-169f6f65-5871-519b-a5b5-58af3670b1d5" :answer/id #uuid "169f6f65-5871-519b-a5b5-58af3670b1d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}^{3}-x+9-\\frac{4}{x+3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-84195c6c-e13d-58c7-8f62-b8364f00b637" :question/id #uuid "84195c6c-e13d-58c7-8f62-b8364f00b637" :question/math-academy-id "q-18577" :question/problem "$\\frac{-{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+x+1}{x+4}=$" :question/worked-solution "We can calculate $\\frac{-{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+x+1}{x+4}$ using synthetic division.\n\nCarrying out the synthetic division process, we arrive at the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{4} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ -4 & -1 & -3 & 4 & 1 & 1 \\\\  & ↓ & 4 & -4 & 0 & -4 \\\\  & -1 & 1 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+x+1}{x+4}=-{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+1-\\frac{3}{x+4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-23231c31-724d-51d7-aa6f-f7ca2083833d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-23231c31-724d-51d7-aa6f-f7ca2083833d" :answer-field/id #uuid "23231c31-724d-51d7-aa6f-f7ca2083833d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0c1bd531-0de7-525b-8300-8cc89c022598" :answer-field/choices ["answer-afba8a58-1017-5f18-bf57-fd6a18b0ee20" "answer-30488cbf-33f4-5e0f-959a-d6e3b556522f" "answer-d659d2fd-291e-5be2-ad56-cfd41202f459" "answer-0c1bd531-0de7-525b-8300-8cc89c022598" "answer-23683e8c-85ff-58cb-b908-b24a1cd95133"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-afba8a58-1017-5f18-bf57-fd6a18b0ee20" :answer/id #uuid "afba8a58-1017-5f18-bf57-fd6a18b0ee20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}-6-\\frac{3}{x+4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-30488cbf-33f4-5e0f-959a-d6e3b556522f" :answer/id #uuid "30488cbf-33f4-5e0f-959a-d6e3b556522f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+12+\\frac{3}{x+4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d659d2fd-291e-5be2-ad56-cfd41202f459" :answer/id #uuid "d659d2fd-291e-5be2-ad56-cfd41202f459" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}+4-\\frac{3}{x+4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0c1bd531-0de7-525b-8300-8cc89c022598" :answer/id #uuid "0c1bd531-0de7-525b-8300-8cc89c022598" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+1-\\frac{3}{x+4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-23683e8c-85ff-58cb-b908-b24a1cd95133" :answer/id #uuid "23683e8c-85ff-58cb-b908-b24a1cd95133" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+21+\\frac{3}{x+4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083204 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-343c6002-3a70-5903-a244-0acddb5859ce"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-343c6002-3a70-5903-a244-0acddb5859ce" :question/id #uuid "343c6002-3a70-5903-a244-0acddb5859ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-73818" :question/problem "$\\frac{9{x}^{4}+12{x}^{3}-25}{3x-5}=$" :question/worked-solution "We can calculate $\\frac{9{x}^{4}+12{x}^{3}-25}{3x-5}$ using synthetic division.\n\nFor synthetic division to work, we need the coefficient of $x$ in the denominator to be equal to $1.$ So first, we factor the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9{x}^{4}+12{x}^{3}-25}{3x-5} & =\\frac{9{x}^{4}+12{x}^{3}-25}{3(x-\\frac{5}{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{9{x}^{4}+12{x}^{3}-25}{(x-\\frac{5}{3})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCarrying out the synthetic division process on $\\frac{9{x}^{4}+12{x}^{3}-25}{(x-\\frac{5}{3})}$, we arrive at the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{4} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ \\frac{5}{3} & 9 & 12 & 0 & 0 & -25 \\\\  & ↓ & 15 & 45 & 75 & 125 \\\\  & 9 & 27 & 45 & 75 & 100\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{9{x}^{4}+12{x}^{3}-25}{(x-\\frac{5}{3})} & =\\frac{1}{3}(9{x}^{3}+27{x}^{2}+45x+75+\\frac{100}{(x-\\frac{5}{3})}) \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}+9{x}^{2}+15x+25+\\frac{100}{3x-5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our final result is\n\n$$\n\\frac{9{x}^{4}+12{x}^{3}-25}{3x-5}=3{x}^{3}+9{x}^{2}+15x+25+\\frac{100}{3x-5}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a916e5ab-d2bf-5c35-99df-efcacc3f8e56"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a916e5ab-d2bf-5c35-99df-efcacc3f8e56" :answer-field/id #uuid "a916e5ab-d2bf-5c35-99df-efcacc3f8e56" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-15c18ebe-c675-5bcf-b34d-fee9f38573de" :answer-field/choices ["answer-62a672e0-4667-5d14-94ed-8c58ba311d8c" "answer-15c18ebe-c675-5bcf-b34d-fee9f38573de" "answer-5afbc067-5499-538e-a8b6-7c624c3edc2e" "answer-d952f828-349f-5d26-a20c-bf66dfa362fd" "answer-af6c1d59-c605-55b7-98a8-43b605decc44"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-62a672e0-4667-5d14-94ed-8c58ba311d8c" :answer/id #uuid "62a672e0-4667-5d14-94ed-8c58ba311d8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}-9x+2-\\frac{100}{3x-5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15c18ebe-c675-5bcf-b34d-fee9f38573de" :answer/id #uuid "15c18ebe-c675-5bcf-b34d-fee9f38573de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}^{3}+9{x}^{2}+15x+25+\\frac{100}{3x-5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5afbc067-5499-538e-a8b6-7c624c3edc2e" :answer/id #uuid "5afbc067-5499-538e-a8b6-7c624c3edc2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}^{3}+9{x}^{2}-15x-50+\\frac{100}{3x-5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d952f828-349f-5d26-a20c-bf66dfa362fd" :answer/id #uuid "d952f828-349f-5d26-a20c-bf66dfa362fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}+9x+21+\\frac{100}{3x-5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af6c1d59-c605-55b7-98a8-43b605decc44" :answer/id #uuid "af6c1d59-c605-55b7-98a8-43b605decc44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+5x+25-\\frac{100}{3x-5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-87369fa2-1336-5ef5-ab81-fdcbdb07cf83" :activity/id #uuid "87369fa2-1336-5ef5-ab81-fdcbdb07cf83" :activity/title "Dividing Polynomials Using Synthetic Division" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186051061 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-5996360f-63a5-5e3f-a0ef-bac173ffcb52" "step-34f2531b-3118-5542-84d9-9e90e68fa910" "step-340e3ed6-35e3-5d45-bca2-83d91ae792ee"] :activity/first-step "step-5996360f-63a5-5e3f-a0ef-bac173ffcb52" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-5996360f-63a5-5e3f-a0ef-bac173ffcb52" :step/id #uuid "5996360f-63a5-5e3f-a0ef-bac173ffcb52" :step/content "question-8ccbfa58-d595-551b-aac0-8c85b253cfbe" :step/next "step-34f2531b-3118-5542-84d9-9e90e68fa910" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-34f2531b-3118-5542-84d9-9e90e68fa910" :step/id #uuid "34f2531b-3118-5542-84d9-9e90e68fa910" :step/content "question-84195c6c-e13d-58c7-8f62-b8364f00b637" :step/next "step-340e3ed6-35e3-5d45-bca2-83d91ae792ee" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-340e3ed6-35e3-5d45-bca2-83d91ae792ee" :step/id #uuid "340e3ed6-35e3-5d45-bca2-83d91ae792ee" :step/content "question-343c6002-3a70-5903-a244-0acddb5859ce" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186220900 :answer-field/choices 17592186220904] [:db/retract 17592186220900 :answer-field/choices 17592186220901] [:db/retract 17592186220900 :answer-field/choices 17592186220902] [:db/retract 17592186220900 :answer-field/choices 17592186220903] {:db/id 17592186221457 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f846bdbb-b4eb-53cc-9341-26d00f9d6239"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186221455 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8a503430-335a-52ca-a8f2-1a25c8b18de5" "question-336eb7d8-27df-584e-adc9-df5d1de8bc4e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8a503430-335a-52ca-a8f2-1a25c8b18de5" :question/id #uuid "8a503430-335a-52ca-a8f2-1a25c8b18de5" :question/math-academy-id "q-343819" :question/problem "Select the missing parts in a particular solution of the differential equation ${y}^{′}+3y=f(x),$ where the Fourier series of the $4$-periodic forcing function is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nThe Fourier series of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-1}}\\cdot cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})+{{field-2}}\\cdot sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We assume that a solution of our equation has the following Fourier series:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})+{b}_{n}sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})+{b}_{n}sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})) \\\\  & ∼0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\cdot (-\\frac{n\\pi }{2}sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}))+{b}_{n}\\cdot \\frac{n\\pi }{2}cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}) \\\\  & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{2}sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})+\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{2}cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{p}^{′}$ and ${y}_{p}$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{2}sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})+\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{2}cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})) \\\\  & \\,+3(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})+{b}_{n}sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})) \\\\  & \\,\\,={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRearranging the terms, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{3{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{2}+3{a}_{n})cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}) \\\\  & \\,\\,+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{2}+3{b}_{n})sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}) \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, equating the free terms and the cosine and sine coefficients, we obtain the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{a}_{0}}{2}=0 \\\\ \\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{2}+3{a}_{n}=0 \\\\ -\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{2}+3{b}_{n}=\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, ${a}_{0}=0.$ \n\nNext, from the second equation, \n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=-\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{6}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the third equation gives\n\n$$\n-(-\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{6})\\frac{n\\pi }{2}+3{b}_{n}=\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }\\,⇒\\,{b}_{n}=\\frac{24(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for ${a}_{n}$ with $n\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =-\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =-\\frac{n\\pi }{6}\\cdot \\frac{24(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,-\\frac{4(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36}\\cdot cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})+\\frac{24(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}\\cdot sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-819e15d7-2e20-52a4-83ba-4e170679fa89" "answer-field-34398e9c-a70c-53b7-b84a-4a5e338eee91"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-819e15d7-2e20-52a4-83ba-4e170679fa89" :answer-field/id #uuid "819e15d7-2e20-52a4-83ba-4e170679fa89" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-ab325d87-a065-546e-baf7-139015307fa0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-30256479-a0c3-536f-992c-58c727330693" "answer-ab325d87-a065-546e-baf7-139015307fa0" "answer-644342fd-f897-5f58-92a1-0b8ef53eb76b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-30256479-a0c3-536f-992c-58c727330693" :answer/id #uuid "30256479-a0c3-536f-992c-58c727330693" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{12(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ab325d87-a065-546e-baf7-139015307fa0" :answer/id #uuid "ab325d87-a065-546e-baf7-139015307fa0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-644342fd-f897-5f58-92a1-0b8ef53eb76b" :answer/id #uuid "644342fd-f897-5f58-92a1-0b8ef53eb76b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-34398e9c-a70c-53b7-b84a-4a5e338eee91" :answer-field/id #uuid "34398e9c-a70c-53b7-b84a-4a5e338eee91" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-85bccb7d-0294-553d-b094-d5837f950d47" :answer-field/choices ["answer-78061c99-9116-56c2-88f4-777413d48782" "answer-f77c27c9-c7d3-591e-bac3-638faae40001" "answer-85bccb7d-0294-553d-b094-d5837f950d47"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78061c99-9116-56c2-88f4-777413d48782" :answer/id #uuid "78061c99-9116-56c2-88f4-777413d48782" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{18(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f77c27c9-c7d3-591e-bac3-638faae40001" :answer/id #uuid "f77c27c9-c7d3-591e-bac3-638faae40001" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{12(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-85bccb7d-0294-553d-b094-d5837f950d47" :answer/id #uuid "85bccb7d-0294-553d-b094-d5837f950d47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{24(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-336eb7d8-27df-584e-adc9-df5d1de8bc4e" :question/id #uuid "336eb7d8-27df-584e-adc9-df5d1de8bc4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-344058" :question/problem "Select the missing parts in a particular solution of the differential equation ${y}^{′}-3y=f(x),$ where the Fourier series of the $6$-periodic forcing function is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼-3+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{6}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\n$$\n\nThe Fourier series of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}∼{{field-1}} & +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\  & +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-3}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We assume that a solution of our equation has the following Fourier series:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})) \\\\  & ∼0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\cdot (-\\frac{n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}))+{b}_{n}\\cdot \\frac{n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\  & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})+\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{p}^{′}$ and ${y}_{p}$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})+\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})) \\\\  & \\,-3(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})) \\\\  & \\,\\,=-3+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{6}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRearranging the terms, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & -3\\cdot \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{3}-3{a}_{n})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\  & \\,\\,+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{3}-3{b}_{n})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,=-3+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{6}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, equating the free terms and the coefficients next to sines and cosines, we obtain the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-3\\cdot \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}=-3 \\\\ \\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{3}-3{a}_{n}=\\frac{6}{{n}^{2}\\pi } \\\\ -\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{3}-3{b}_{n}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, ${a}_{0}=2,$ which means the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNext, from the third equation, \n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{9}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation gives\n\n$$\n(-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{9})\\frac{n\\pi }{3}-3{a}_{n}=\\frac{6}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\,⇒\\,{a}_{n}=-\\frac{162}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, for ${a}_{n}$ with $n\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{n} & =-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{9} \\\\  & =-\\frac{n\\pi }{9}\\cdot (-\\frac{162}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}∼1 & +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,-\\frac{162}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81)}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\  & +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{18}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81)}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-319f9cc5-6350-50bc-9ef5-9fc966e9afe8" "answer-field-cdd62ed7-f5a0-5d14-b295-af477d1b5a66" "answer-field-44914850-8fa0-5396-b873-81fa2f52fbd0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-319f9cc5-6350-50bc-9ef5-9fc966e9afe8" :answer-field/id #uuid "319f9cc5-6350-50bc-9ef5-9fc966e9afe8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-efdbe697-d6a3-508c-a692-ae48f85ba690" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b7737c7e-9824-5e5f-a3ae-34856a098e7c" "answer-ab11db4e-65b6-5238-aa40-285ffcaa4e1d" "answer-efdbe697-d6a3-508c-a692-ae48f85ba690" "answer-55053340-f635-546e-8e5d-4621e256edb8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b7737c7e-9824-5e5f-a3ae-34856a098e7c" :answer/id #uuid "b7737c7e-9824-5e5f-a3ae-34856a098e7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ab11db4e-65b6-5238-aa40-285ffcaa4e1d" :answer/id #uuid "ab11db4e-65b6-5238-aa40-285ffcaa4e1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-efdbe697-d6a3-508c-a692-ae48f85ba690" :answer/id #uuid "efdbe697-d6a3-508c-a692-ae48f85ba690" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-55053340-f635-546e-8e5d-4621e256edb8" :answer/id #uuid "55053340-f635-546e-8e5d-4621e256edb8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cdd62ed7-f5a0-5d14-b295-af477d1b5a66" :answer-field/id #uuid "cdd62ed7-f5a0-5d14-b295-af477d1b5a66" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-92481f36-1e85-521a-ba9a-acee004b176f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-92481f36-1e85-521a-ba9a-acee004b176f" "answer-46ca47af-c6a7-509f-8d83-2150c0238a78" "answer-e0c34785-8282-5217-a833-be2afab68c64"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92481f36-1e85-521a-ba9a-acee004b176f" :answer/id #uuid "92481f36-1e85-521a-ba9a-acee004b176f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{162}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-46ca47af-c6a7-509f-8d83-2150c0238a78" :answer/id #uuid "46ca47af-c6a7-509f-8d83-2150c0238a78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{18}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e0c34785-8282-5217-a833-be2afab68c64" :answer/id #uuid "e0c34785-8282-5217-a833-be2afab68c64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{162}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-44914850-8fa0-5396-b873-81fa2f52fbd0" :answer-field/id #uuid "44914850-8fa0-5396-b873-81fa2f52fbd0" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-e29b2edf-998e-5740-bb95-54727e9f45f8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e29b2edf-998e-5740-bb95-54727e9f45f8" "answer-1b3542e3-4bf3-5d25-87cb-feba5f3ffd90" "answer-5558f4a3-3994-5897-8ff9-622d5df04392"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e29b2edf-998e-5740-bb95-54727e9f45f8" :answer/id #uuid "e29b2edf-998e-5740-bb95-54727e9f45f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{18}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1b3542e3-4bf3-5d25-87cb-feba5f3ffd90" :answer/id #uuid "1b3542e3-4bf3-5d25-87cb-feba5f3ffd90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{18}{{n}^{2}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5558f4a3-3994-5897-8ff9-622d5df04392" :answer/id #uuid "5558f4a3-3994-5897-8ff9-622d5df04392" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186222035 :question/problem "Select the missing parts in a particular solution of the differential equation ${y}^{″}-9y=f(x),$ where the Fourier series of the $2$-periodic forcing function is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\pi }{{n}^{3}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the free term and all the sine coefficients in the Fourier series of the particular solution are equal to zero.*\n\nThe Fourier series of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-1}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We assume that a solution of our equation has the following Fourier series:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x))∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}n\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x) \\\\ {y}_{p}^{″} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}n\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x))∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{p}^{″}$ and ${y}_{p}$ into the equation and have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)-9({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x))={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\pi }{{n}^{3}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\nRearranging the terms, we get \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+9)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\pi }{{n}^{3}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\nNow, equating the cosine coefficients, we obtain \n\n$$\n-{a}_{n}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+9)=\\frac{\\pi }{{n}^{3}}\\,⇒\\,{a}_{n}=-\\frac{\\pi }{{n}^{3}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+9)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{{n}^{3}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+9)}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186220900 :answer-field/correct "answer-569abf23-828d-556a-8f5f-a80cd2b16ce5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ec30d690-d89c-5e99-97e6-bdae59c5d3d2" "answer-569abf23-828d-556a-8f5f-a80cd2b16ce5" "answer-ff05bb1d-0d47-5a0b-9d42-84f03013e335" "answer-a4c02cbf-419a-5b32-acdf-ac8babf2fa7a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ec30d690-d89c-5e99-97e6-bdae59c5d3d2" :answer/id #uuid "ec30d690-d89c-5e99-97e6-bdae59c5d3d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{n({n}^{3}\\pi -9)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-569abf23-828d-556a-8f5f-a80cd2b16ce5" :answer/id #uuid "569abf23-828d-556a-8f5f-a80cd2b16ce5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{{n}^{3}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+9)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff05bb1d-0d47-5a0b-9d42-84f03013e335" :answer/id #uuid "ff05bb1d-0d47-5a0b-9d42-84f03013e335" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{n}^{3}{\\pi }^{2}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}-9)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a4c02cbf-419a-5b32-acdf-ac8babf2fa7a" :answer/id #uuid "a4c02cbf-419a-5b32-acdf-ac8babf2fa7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{n+1}{{n}^{3}{\\pi }^{2}+9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f846bdbb-b4eb-53cc-9341-26d00f9d6239" :question/id #uuid "f846bdbb-b4eb-53cc-9341-26d00f9d6239" :question/math-academy-id "q-343906" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation ${y}^{″}+{\\pi }^{2}y=f(x),$ where the $2$-periodic forcing function is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼4+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{9}{{n}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below regarding the resonant component of a particular solution of the equation.\n\nThe natural frequency of the system matches the frequency of the {{field-1}} harmonic of the forcing function. \n\nConsequently, the particular solution contains a resonant term of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{1}}={{field-2}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We begin by identifying resonance. The differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\pi }^{2}y=f(x)\n$$\n\nhas a natural frequency of \n\n$$\n\\omega =\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}}=\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe frequencies of the forcing harmonics for a $2$-periodic function $(L=1)$ are \n\n$$\n{\\omega }_{n}=\\frac{n\\pi }{1}=n\\pi .\n$$\n\nFor $n=1$, we have ${\\omega }_{1}=\\pi .$ Since ${\\omega }_{1}=\\omega ,$ the $n=1$ harmonic of the forcing function causes resonance.\n\nFor the $n=1$ harmonic, the forcing term is \n\n$$\n{f}_{1}(x)=9\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x).\n$$\n\nBecause this frequency matches the natural frequency, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{1}}=x(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{{p}_{1}}^{′} & =(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x))+x(-\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)+\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)) \\\\ {y}_{{p}_{1}}^{″} & =-2\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)+2\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)-{\\pi }^{2}x(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{{p}_{1}}^{″}$ and ${y}_{{p}_{1}}$ into the equation ${y}^{″}+{\\pi }^{2}y=9\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x):$\n\n$$\n[-2\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)+2\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)-{\\pi }^{2}{y}_{{p}_{1}}]+{\\pi }^{2}{y}_{{p}_{1}}=9\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)\n$$\n\nThe resonant terms involving $x$ cancel out, leaving\n\n$$\n-2\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)+2\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)=9\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x).\n$$\n\nNow, equating the sine and cosine coefficients, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-2\\pi A=9 \\\\ 2\\pi B=0\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}A=-\\frac{9}{2\\pi } \\\\ B=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the resonant component of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{1}}=-\\frac{9x}{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8ce88b2e-b185-5d2e-8cfe-5be89cc0aa87" "answer-field-1e995e02-d0ce-5ccb-a037-04ceee50e084"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8ce88b2e-b185-5d2e-8cfe-5be89cc0aa87" :answer-field/id #uuid "8ce88b2e-b185-5d2e-8cfe-5be89cc0aa87" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-ccea3e9e-29c1-513f-99b9-7b21823c4113" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ccea3e9e-29c1-513f-99b9-7b21823c4113" "answer-27429d6e-d26b-57af-88d8-b3b645dceff5" "answer-83ac4344-49cc-52a5-af95-e3d90acd43a2" "answer-5774f527-99ad-5f17-a48d-89c6006f3a3d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ccea3e9e-29c1-513f-99b9-7b21823c4113" :answer/id #uuid "ccea3e9e-29c1-513f-99b9-7b21823c4113" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-27429d6e-d26b-57af-88d8-b3b645dceff5" :answer/id #uuid "27429d6e-d26b-57af-88d8-b3b645dceff5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-83ac4344-49cc-52a5-af95-e3d90acd43a2" :answer/id #uuid "83ac4344-49cc-52a5-af95-e3d90acd43a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5774f527-99ad-5f17-a48d-89c6006f3a3d" :answer/id #uuid "5774f527-99ad-5f17-a48d-89c6006f3a3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1e995e02-d0ce-5ccb-a037-04ceee50e084" :answer-field/id #uuid "1e995e02-d0ce-5ccb-a037-04ceee50e084" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-a4ade4ea-e129-57c8-abf7-ee1ae4a37fe1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a4ade4ea-e129-57c8-abf7-ee1ae4a37fe1" "answer-65f57259-781b-593f-95c6-d5d30ac088ef" "answer-a913ed3d-a5ff-575d-afb5-86ec312e2921" "answer-23e85abf-8716-50e3-935c-317dbb984f0b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a4ade4ea-e129-57c8-abf7-ee1ae4a37fe1" :answer/id #uuid "a4ade4ea-e129-57c8-abf7-ee1ae4a37fe1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{9x}{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-65f57259-781b-593f-95c6-d5d30ac088ef" :answer/id #uuid "65f57259-781b-593f-95c6-d5d30ac088ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{9x}{4\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a913ed3d-a5ff-575d-afb5-86ec312e2921" :answer/id #uuid "a913ed3d-a5ff-575d-afb5-86ec312e2921" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{9x}{8\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-23e85abf-8716-50e3-935c-317dbb984f0b" :answer/id #uuid "23e85abf-8716-50e3-935c-317dbb984f0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9x}{4\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186132373 :answer-field/choices 17592186132374] [:db/retract 17592186132373 :answer-field/choices 17592186132375] [:db/retract 17592186132373 :answer-field/choices 17592186132376] [:db/retract 17592186132373 :answer-field/choices 17592186132377] [:db/retract 17592186132373 :answer-field/choices 17592186132378] {:db/id 17592186133807 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-789ea0d3-54ac-52af-9aa3-c806bd076e69"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133616 :question/problem "| $x$ | **$0$** | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $5$ | $2$ |\n\nConsider the data above and the matrices below. Find an expression (in terms of $X$ and $\\mathbf{y}$) for the vector of coefficients $\\boldsymbol{\\beta}$ of the curve $y=\\beta_0 + \\beta_1 x + \\beta_2 x^2 + \\beta_3 x^3$ that best fits the data. \n\n![](images/17/172f8147d4d58d4d3edc42f96e3fb248f59cb749ed0e387c9c8bcddfec08bf79.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-789ea0d3-54ac-52af-9aa3-c806bd076e69" :question/id #uuid "789ea0d3-54ac-52af-9aa3-c806bd076e69" :question/math-academy-id "q-139599" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$0$** | **$2$** | **$4$** | **$6$** | **$8$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-1$ | $2$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $3$ |\n\nConsider the data above and the matrices below. Find an expression for the vector of coefficients of the curve $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}+{\\beta }_{3}{x}^{3}$ that best fits the data. \n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & {0}^{2} & {0}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 2 & {2}^{2} & {2}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 4 & {4}^{2} & {4}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 6 & {6}^{2} & {6}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 8 & {8}^{2} & {8}^{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,\\beta =[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2} \\\\ {\\beta }_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The coefficients of the curve \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}+{\\beta }_{3}{x}^{3}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\nX\\beta =y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector.\n\nPre-multiplying this equation by ${X}^{T},$ we obtain the corresponding normal equation\n\n$$\n{X}^{T}\\,X\\overset{^}{\\beta }={X}^{T}y.\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $X$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${X}^{T}X$ is invertible and \n\n$$\n\\overset{^}{\\beta }=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b5f5769d-1629-52ad-a8ed-38afe0f42079"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b5f5769d-1629-52ad-a8ed-38afe0f42079" :answer-field/id #uuid "b5f5769d-1629-52ad-a8ed-38afe0f42079" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6ca78b37-8471-59f6-984c-04f09b456143" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a5d7a022-1c16-5e7b-ba63-b8d6ebd79ac5" "answer-ffaf612d-85b8-52f9-bacb-05a3a72950b8" "answer-6ca78b37-8471-59f6-984c-04f09b456143" "answer-28ecf387-c091-569b-870f-de70138cb197" "answer-021af7c8-298c-5829-b9fa-fc8322b9f50d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5d7a022-1c16-5e7b-ba63-b8d6ebd79ac5" :answer/id #uuid "a5d7a022-1c16-5e7b-ba63-b8d6ebd79ac5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(X{X}^{T})^{-1}X{X}^{T}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ffaf612d-85b8-52f9-bacb-05a3a72950b8" :answer/id #uuid "ffaf612d-85b8-52f9-bacb-05a3a72950b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}\\,Xy" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ca78b37-8471-59f6-984c-04f09b456143" :answer/id #uuid "6ca78b37-8471-59f6-984c-04f09b456143" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-28ecf387-c091-569b-870f-de70138cb197" :answer/id #uuid "28ecf387-c091-569b-870f-de70138cb197" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "X({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-021af7c8-298c-5829-b9fa-fc8322b9f50d" :answer/id #uuid "021af7c8-298c-5829-b9fa-fc8322b9f50d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "X({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133823 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d9bbc936-cdf8-5bb2-be25-3df4f1bc3232"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d9bbc936-cdf8-5bb2-be25-3df4f1bc3232" :question/id #uuid "d9bbc936-cdf8-5bb2-be25-3df4f1bc3232" :question/math-academy-id "q-139653" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$-3$** | **$-1$** | **$1$** | **$3$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-5$ | $-25$ | $5$ | $20$ | $35$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients of the curve $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}$ that best fits the data above can be found using polynomial regression as \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{aligned}]=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the observation vector $y$ in this context?" :question/worked-solution "| $x$ | **$-3$** | **$-1$** | **$1$** | **$3$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-5$ | $-25$ | $5$ | $20$ | $35$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the curve \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & (-3)^{2} \\\\ 1 & -1 & (-1)^{2} \\\\ 1 & 1 & {1}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 3 & {3}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 5 & {5}^{2}\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -25 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 35\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b4aab56a-66ce-5d92-bf05-9bff500864c1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b4aab56a-66ce-5d92-bf05-9bff500864c1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b4aab56a-66ce-5d92-bf05-9bff500864c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a61433c9-2b22-57c8-9478-14e323e7d6b6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a348d2b4-ce93-5a99-a6ed-1906d407475a" "answer-65dd863d-70c0-5170-aa9a-00b0ab5e1a31" "answer-625975e6-7869-5a67-bc59-519fa2d8371d" "answer-a61433c9-2b22-57c8-9478-14e323e7d6b6" "answer-a6559ef5-d440-5051-9b33-5e541b8f53b5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a348d2b4-ce93-5a99-a6ed-1906d407475a" :answer/id #uuid "a348d2b4-ce93-5a99-a6ed-1906d407475a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}(-3)^{2} \\\\ (-1)^{2} \\\\ {1}^{2} \\\\ {3}^{2} \\\\ {5}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-65dd863d-70c0-5170-aa9a-00b0ab5e1a31" :answer/id #uuid "65dd863d-70c0-5170-aa9a-00b0ab5e1a31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}(-5)^{2} \\\\ (-25)^{2} \\\\ {5}^{2} \\\\ {20}^{2} \\\\ {35}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-625975e6-7869-5a67-bc59-519fa2d8371d" :answer/id #uuid "625975e6-7869-5a67-bc59-519fa2d8371d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a61433c9-2b22-57c8-9478-14e323e7d6b6" :answer/id #uuid "a61433c9-2b22-57c8-9478-14e323e7d6b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -25 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 35\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6559ef5-d440-5051-9b33-5e541b8f53b5" :answer/id #uuid "a6559ef5-d440-5051-9b33-5e541b8f53b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134389 :question/problem "| $x$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients of the curve $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}+{\\beta }_{3}{x}^{3}$ that best fits the data above can be found using polynomial regression as \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2} \\\\ {\\beta }_{3}\\end{aligned}]=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the design matrix $X$ in this context?" :question/worked-solution "| $x$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the curve \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}+{\\beta }_{3}{x}^{3}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & {1}^{2} & {1}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 2 & {2}^{2} & {2}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 3 & {3}^{2} & {3}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 4 & {4}^{2} & {4}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 5 & {5}^{2} & {5}^{3}\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2} \\\\ {\\beta }_{3}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186132373 :answer-field/correct "answer-8f5c471a-3743-58fa-b032-6489b39478a8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8f5c471a-3743-58fa-b032-6489b39478a8" "answer-aec9c374-1a4f-55d4-a0d4-1da3da5ab4af" "answer-2ab6240c-a811-5ed5-a876-ef55a74dd515" "answer-f6744f4c-62ff-5cd6-b5e9-04b41d3ac340" "answer-dfd58429-3797-5a27-8e39-d9edfc6a019f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f5c471a-3743-58fa-b032-6489b39478a8" :answer/id #uuid "8f5c471a-3743-58fa-b032-6489b39478a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & {1}^{2} & {1}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 2 & {2}^{2} & {2}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 3 & {3}^{2} & {3}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 4 & {4}^{2} & {4}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 5 & {5}^{2} & {5}^{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aec9c374-1a4f-55d4-a0d4-1da3da5ab4af" :answer/id #uuid "aec9c374-1a4f-55d4-a0d4-1da3da5ab4af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ab6240c-a811-5ed5-a876-ef55a74dd515" :answer/id #uuid "2ab6240c-a811-5ed5-a876-ef55a74dd515" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f6744f4c-62ff-5cd6-b5e9-04b41d3ac340" :answer/id #uuid "f6744f4c-62ff-5cd6-b5e9-04b41d3ac340" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dfd58429-3797-5a27-8e39-d9edfc6a019f" :answer/id #uuid "dfd58429-3797-5a27-8e39-d9edfc6a019f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133806 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1dfba625-81c0-581d-a463-4b6d422c9f73"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-1dfba625-81c0-581d-a463-4b6d422c9f73" :question/id #uuid "1dfba625-81c0-581d-a463-4b6d422c9f73" :question/math-academy-id "q-139660" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$0$** | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $15$ | $19$ | $14$ | $-9$ | $-11$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients of the curve $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}+{\\beta }_{3}{x}^{3}$ that best fits the data above can be found using polynomial regression as \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2} \\\\ {\\beta }_{3}\\end{aligned}]=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the design matrix $X$ in this context?" :question/worked-solution "| $x$ | **$0$** | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $15$ | $19$ | $14$ | $-9$ | $-11$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the curve \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}+{\\beta }_{3}{x}^{3}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & {0}^{2} & {0}^{3} \\\\ 1 & {1}^{2} & {1}^{3} \\\\ 1 & {2}^{2} & {2}^{3} \\\\ 1 & {3}^{2} & {3}^{3} \\\\ 1 & {4}^{2} & {4}^{3}\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2} \\\\ {\\beta }_{3}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 19 \\\\ 14 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e5c23c67-d5f0-5435-9ff0-f58fa6b0cfc8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e5c23c67-d5f0-5435-9ff0-f58fa6b0cfc8" :answer-field/id #uuid "e5c23c67-d5f0-5435-9ff0-f58fa6b0cfc8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9ebfa448-95fd-50cb-8944-07f3949c13df" :answer-field/choices ["answer-702d8457-7a04-5f81-b354-457a65777dea" "answer-41265bdd-d701-5915-85ea-b8b48d3032b4" "answer-9ebfa448-95fd-50cb-8944-07f3949c13df" "answer-bd434e23-296a-58e6-8c06-72a49aab1760" "answer-a181d0c5-2f8c-57a8-860d-c4b8dd85032a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-702d8457-7a04-5f81-b354-457a65777dea" :answer/id #uuid "702d8457-7a04-5f81-b354-457a65777dea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & {0}^{2} & {0}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 1 & {1}^{2} & {1}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 2 & {2}^{2} & {2}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 3 & {3}^{2} & {3}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 4 & {4}^{2} & {4}^{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41265bdd-d701-5915-85ea-b8b48d3032b4" :answer/id #uuid "41265bdd-d701-5915-85ea-b8b48d3032b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & {0}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 1 & {1}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 2 & {2}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 3 & {3}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 4 & {4}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9ebfa448-95fd-50cb-8944-07f3949c13df" :answer/id #uuid "9ebfa448-95fd-50cb-8944-07f3949c13df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & {0}^{2} & {0}^{3} \\\\ 1 & {1}^{2} & {1}^{3} \\\\ 1 & {2}^{2} & {2}^{3} \\\\ 1 & {3}^{2} & {3}^{3} \\\\ 1 & {4}^{2} & {4}^{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd434e23-296a-58e6-8c06-72a49aab1760" :answer/id #uuid "bd434e23-296a-58e6-8c06-72a49aab1760" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}15 & 0 & {0}^{2} \\\\ 19 & 1 & {1}^{2} \\\\ 14 & 2 & {2}^{2} \\\\ -9 & 3 & {3}^{2} \\\\ -11 & 4 & {4}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a181d0c5-2f8c-57a8-860d-c4b8dd85032a" :answer/id #uuid "a181d0c5-2f8c-57a8-860d-c4b8dd85032a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}15 & {0}^{2} & {0}^{3} \\\\ 19 & {1}^{2} & {1}^{3} \\\\ 14 & {2}^{2} & {2}^{3} \\\\ -9 & {3}^{2} & {3}^{3} \\\\ -11 & {4}^{2} & {4}^{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186135063 :tutorial/content "We've seen how to construct a simple linear regression model given some bivariate data $(x,y).$ We can generalize this technique to fit data to an arbitrary polynomial. We call this process **polynomial regression**.\n\nThe following table gives the number of units $x$ (in hundreds) produced by a small company and the respective profits $y$ (in thousands of dollars) earned for producing $x$ units:\n\n| Goods $(x)$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Profit $(y)$ | $16$ | $11$ | $15$ | $18$ |\n\nSuppose we want to find the quadratic function\n\n$$\ny = \\beta_0 + \\beta_1 x + \\beta_2 x^2\n$$\n\nthat best fits the given data points.\n\n![](images/93/93fe1784b89ce4c892c84a03a0dc80909f16f46ac463c5cc30b40f869a7802bf.png)\n\nSubstituting the values of $x$ into the regression equation and equating the results to the corresponding observed values of $y,$ we obtain the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0}+1{\\beta }_{1}+{1}^{2}{\\beta }_{2}=16 \\\\ {\\beta }_{0}+2{\\beta }_{1}+{2}^{2}{\\beta }_{2}=11 \\\\ {\\beta }_{0}+3{\\beta }_{1}+{3}^{2}{\\beta }_{2}=15 \\\\ {\\beta }_{0}+4{\\beta }_{1}+{4}^{2}{\\beta }_{2}=18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis system can be written using matrix notation as\n\n![](images/72/729e20ddab6e49b109ebccbb049b1abb9ca2fc11003a9e7f4828bff305a283b4.svg)\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\boldsymbol{\\beta}$ is the parameter vector, and $\\mathbf{y}$ is the observation vector. \n\nSince our points do not lie on a quadratic curve, there will be no parameters $\\beta_0, \\beta_1,$ and $\\beta_2$ such that this equation is true. So instead, we seek parameters $\\beta_0, \\beta_1,$ and $\\beta_2$ that best approximate the solution.\n\nIn other words, we seek to find a column vector $\\boldsymbol\\beta$ such that\n\n$$\n\\| \\mathbf{y} - X\\boldsymbol{\\beta}\\|\n$$\n\nis as small as possible.\n\nNotice that this is exactly the least-squares problem for the system $X \\boldsymbol{\\beta} = \\mathbf{y}.$ Therefore, the coefficients of the curve that best fits the data can be found as the solution to the corresponding least-squares problem! \n\nPre-multiplying the equation $X \\boldsymbol{\\beta} = \\mathbf{y}$ by $X^T,$ we obtain the corresponding normal equation\n\n$$\nX^T \\! X {\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\beta}}} = X^T \\mathbf{y}.\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $X$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${X^T}X$ is invertible, and \n\n$$\n{\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\beta}}} = (X^T \\! X )^{-1} X^T \\mathbf{y}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $X$ and $\\mathbf{y}$ into the formula above and simplifying, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{\\beta }=[\\begin{aligned}22.5 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the quadratic curve of best fit (regression curve) is \n\n$$\ny = 22.5 - 9x + 2x^2.\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186135144 :tutorial/content "In some cases, we might need to constrain the regression curve so that some of its coefficients equal zero. \n\nConsider the table below, which gives the number of units $x$ (in hundreds) produced by a small company and the respective profits $y$ (in thousands of dollars) earned for producing $x$ units. \n\n| Goods $(x)$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Profit $(y)$ | $2$ | $5$ | $8$ | $18$ |\n\nIt's known that the profit equals zero when the company does not produce any goods, so $y=0$ when $x=0.$ The company wishes to find a *quadratic* curve that best fits the data *subject to* the constraint that it should pass through the point $(0,0).$\n\nSo, our regression curve must pass through the point $(0,0).$ In other words, the $y$-intercept of the quadratic curve must be $0.$ Therefore, we want to find the quadratic function\n\n$$\ny = \\beta_1 x + \\beta_2 x^2\n$$\n\nthat best fits the given data points.\n\n![](images/0f/0f98711850478ba6a152103452446e1b2a97ca64c2d47ab7c257db2d05335fcf.png)\n\nSubstituting the values of $x$ into the regression equation and equating the results to the corresponding observed values of $y,$ we obtain the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{1}+{1}^{2}{\\beta }_{2}=2 \\\\ 2{\\beta }_{1}+{2}^{2}{\\beta }_{2}=5 \\\\ 3{\\beta }_{1}+{3}^{2}{\\beta }_{2}=8 \\\\ 4{\\beta }_{1}+{4}^{2}{\\beta }_{2}=18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis system can be written using matrix notation as\n\n![](images/ed/ed2c245e39c03d6d60500866bba6daf37c4e86becb570720b3c6e65aad90720e.svg)\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\boldsymbol{\\beta}$ is the parameter vector, and $\\mathbf{y}$ is the observation vector. \n\nThe rest of the arguments are the same as before. Since our points do not lie on a quadratic curve, there will be no parameters $\\beta_1$ and $\\beta_2$ such that this equation is true. So instead, we seek parameters $\\beta_1$ and $\\beta_2$ that best approximate the solution." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134030 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157326 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-92424f72-7efe-5e04-9bfc-7a9f038c16a4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157325 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8481b6c8-6c2f-5c14-9d27-cfb104ac96ac"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8481b6c8-6c2f-5c14-9d27-cfb104ac96ac" :question/id #uuid "8481b6c8-6c2f-5c14-9d27-cfb104ac96ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-102969" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $\\operatorname{log}⁡(4x-6)-1\\le 0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the logarithm:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{log}⁡(4x-6)-1 & \\le 0 \\\\ \\operatorname{log}⁡(4x-6) & \\le 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use each side of the inequality as an exponent of $10.$ We get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{10}^{\\operatorname{log}⁡(4x-6)} & \\le {10}^{1} \\\\ 4x-6 & \\le 10 \\\\ 4x & \\le 16 \\\\ x & \\le 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we must only keep the solutions that are in the domain of the logarithm in the original inequality. To find the domain of the logarithm, we recall that the argument of the logarithm must be positive:\n\n$$\n4x-6>0\\,⇒\\,x>\\frac{3}{2}\n$$\n\nOur solution is $x\\le 4,$ which can be expressed as $(-\\infty ,4].$ Additionally, the domain of the logarithm is $x>\\frac{3}{2},$ which can be expressed as $(\\frac{3}{2},\\infty ).$ To find the solutions that are in the domain of the logarithm, we take the intersection:\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,4]\\cap (\\frac{3}{2},\\infty )=(\\frac{3}{2},4]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\in (\\frac{3}{2},4],$ which can also be written as $\\frac{3}{2}<x\\le 4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e18b7c6d-9749-540d-b213-14545e6e192e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e18b7c6d-9749-540d-b213-14545e6e192e" :answer-field/id #uuid "e18b7c6d-9749-540d-b213-14545e6e192e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9d0373e9-be0d-5009-bd2d-58b4e3680848" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9f377174-321b-51c2-9b47-d9c6d30ff91a" "answer-6ca4580c-78ff-5453-9ce1-a8788f4f9859" "answer-9d0373e9-be0d-5009-bd2d-58b4e3680848" "answer-7f412de1-636e-540e-9c7c-6b868deaf7ca" "answer-23e72f08-85f6-5f66-b762-41da1e11ea3f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f377174-321b-51c2-9b47-d9c6d30ff91a" :answer/id #uuid "9f377174-321b-51c2-9b47-d9c6d30ff91a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0\\le x<\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ca4580c-78ff-5453-9ce1-a8788f4f9859" :answer/id #uuid "6ca4580c-78ff-5453-9ce1-a8788f4f9859" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\le x\\le 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d0373e9-be0d-5009-bd2d-58b4e3680848" :answer/id #uuid "9d0373e9-be0d-5009-bd2d-58b4e3680848" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}<x\\le 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7f412de1-636e-540e-9c7c-6b868deaf7ca" :answer/id #uuid "7f412de1-636e-540e-9c7c-6b868deaf7ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x>\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-23e72f08-85f6-5f66-b762-41da1e11ea3f" :answer/id #uuid "23e72f08-85f6-5f66-b762-41da1e11ea3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\le 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-92424f72-7efe-5e04-9bfc-7a9f038c16a4" :question/id #uuid "92424f72-7efe-5e04-9bfc-7a9f038c16a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-278762" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)\\ge \\operatorname{ln}⁡(4-2x)-3.$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$x\\,<$\n{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "We use each side of the inequality as an exponent of $e.$ This gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)} & \\ge {e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4-2x)-3} \\\\ {e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)} & \\ge {e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4-2x)}\\cdot {e}^{-3} \\\\ (x+1) & \\ge (4-2x)\\cdot \\frac{1}{{e}^{3}} \\\\ {e}^{3}(x+1) & \\ge 4-2x \\\\ x{e}^{3}+{e}^{3} & \\ge 4-2x \\\\ {e}^{3}-4 & \\ge -2x-x{e}^{3} \\\\ {e}^{3}-4 & \\ge -x(2+{e}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{{e}^{3}-4}{2+{e}^{3}} & \\ge -x \\\\ x & \\ge \\frac{4-{e}^{3}}{2+{e}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we must only keep the solutions that are in the domain of the logarithms in the original inequality. To find the domain of the logarithms, we recall that the argument of the logarithm must be positive:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & >0 & ⇒ &  & x & >-1 \\\\ 4-2x & >0 & ⇒ &  & x & <2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur solution is $x\\ge \\frac{4-{e}^{3}}{2+{e}^{3}},$ which can be expressed as $[\\frac{4-{e}^{3}}{2+{e}^{3}},\\infty ).$ Additionally, the domains of the logarithms are $x>-1$ and $x<2,$ which can be expressed as $(-1,\\infty )$ and $(-\\infty ,2)$ respectively. To find the solutions that are in the domains of the logarithms, we take the intersection:\n\n$$\n[\\frac{4-{e}^{3}}{2+{e}^{3}},\\infty )\\cap (-1,\\infty )\\cap (-\\infty ,2)=[\\frac{4-{e}^{3}}{2+{e}^{3}},2)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\in [\\frac{4-{e}^{3}}{2+{e}^{3}},2),$ which can also be written as \n\n$$\n\\frac{4-{e}^{3}}{2+{e}^{3}}\\le x<2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5858f7d1-e301-50d1-b011-9da4a3416c26" "answer-field-9968bc2f-9867-513c-ae9b-79542778143e" "answer-field-f710cb7f-fb60-597f-b6be-d1109c09f579"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5858f7d1-e301-50d1-b011-9da4a3416c26" :answer-field/id #uuid "5858f7d1-e301-50d1-b011-9da4a3416c26" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-58aa7434-1b75-5cd1-8436-fe2c93b526fe" :answer-field/choices ["answer-58aa7434-1b75-5cd1-8436-fe2c93b526fe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-58aa7434-1b75-5cd1-8436-fe2c93b526fe" :answer/id #uuid "58aa7434-1b75-5cd1-8436-fe2c93b526fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4-e^{3}}{e^{3}+2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9968bc2f-9867-513c-ae9b-79542778143e" :answer-field/id #uuid "9968bc2f-9867-513c-ae9b-79542778143e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-7a940535-172d-5061-a7d3-296375a0780d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7a940535-172d-5061-a7d3-296375a0780d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a940535-172d-5061-a7d3-296375a0780d" :answer/id #uuid "7a940535-172d-5061-a7d3-296375a0780d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\le" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f710cb7f-fb60-597f-b6be-d1109c09f579" :answer-field/id #uuid "f710cb7f-fb60-597f-b6be-d1109c09f579" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d9f776f3-4e02-543e-90c3-d17be3571b5c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d9f776f3-4e02-543e-90c3-d17be3571b5c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d9f776f3-4e02-543e-90c3-d17be3571b5c" :answer/id #uuid "d9f776f3-4e02-543e-90c3-d17be3571b5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-ac6c8ac2-9311-558d-affb-34ac0ff1b5a7" :activity/id #uuid "ac6c8ac2-9311-558d-affb-34ac0ff1b5a7" :activity/title "Solving Inequalities Involving Logarithmic Functions" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049649 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-f63d784a-8428-5b92-a092-6bb3fc08f806" "step-01b4628b-63b7-5c96-87a8-416f13d0e71b" "step-7ad0c79d-a07d-5955-a826-e1237e7efffa" "step-853a46a5-5093-5464-ac8e-f2f6917d8679" "step-c19cdb3a-6668-50f6-9889-77ce12a1e6b9"] :activity/first-step "step-f63d784a-8428-5b92-a092-6bb3fc08f806" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-f63d784a-8428-5b92-a092-6bb3fc08f806" :step/id #uuid "f63d784a-8428-5b92-a092-6bb3fc08f806" :step/content 17592186157906 :step/next "step-01b4628b-63b7-5c96-87a8-416f13d0e71b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-01b4628b-63b7-5c96-87a8-416f13d0e71b" :step/id #uuid "01b4628b-63b7-5c96-87a8-416f13d0e71b" :step/content 17592186354621 :step/next "step-7ad0c79d-a07d-5955-a826-e1237e7efffa" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-7ad0c79d-a07d-5955-a826-e1237e7efffa" :step/id #uuid "7ad0c79d-a07d-5955-a826-e1237e7efffa" :step/content "question-8481b6c8-6c2f-5c14-9d27-cfb104ac96ac" :step/next "step-853a46a5-5093-5464-ac8e-f2f6917d8679" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-853a46a5-5093-5464-ac8e-f2f6917d8679" :step/id #uuid "853a46a5-5093-5464-ac8e-f2f6917d8679" :step/content 17592186294887 :step/next "step-c19cdb3a-6668-50f6-9889-77ce12a1e6b9" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c19cdb3a-6668-50f6-9889-77ce12a1e6b9" :step/id #uuid "c19cdb3a-6668-50f6-9889-77ce12a1e6b9" :step/content "question-92424f72-7efe-5e04-9bfc-7a9f038c16a4" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186122132 :answer-field/choices 17592186122133] [:db/retract 17592186122132 :answer-field/choices 17592186122134] [:db/retract 17592186122132 :answer-field/choices 17592186122135] [:db/retract 17592186122132 :answer-field/choices 17592186122136] [:db/retract 17592186122132 :answer-field/choices 17592186122137] {:db/id 17592186124544 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7d2bfda5-1f22-5eca-90c5-42502b97859c" "question-1cf7f6b8-f438-52c0-a338-61f2ad7fa03e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124353 :question/worked-solution "We are given the following situation for each year: \n\n- $35\\%$ of people who used their own vehicles swap to public transport. This implies that $65\\%$ of them remain using their own vehicles.\n\n- $25\\%$ of people who used public transport swap to their own vehicles. This implies that $75\\%$ of them remain using public transport.\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"2\">From:</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"60\"><b>Vehicles</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"60\"><b>Public Transport </b></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">To:</td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"60\"><b>Vehicles</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.65$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"60\"><b>Public Transport</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.35$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.75$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nNote that we can write a corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n![](images/f9/f91ceb948ae8dadf7a0ce4750d28e6550a996ce7adeb13e63d6622d5a273625b.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124614 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-718b908f-f156-56c4-954e-a24b1b0d0bf9" "question-55574236-41f2-5d82-abc0-f140064784e6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-718b908f-f156-56c4-954e-a24b1b0d0bf9" :question/id #uuid "718b908f-f156-56c4-954e-a24b1b0d0bf9" :question/math-academy-id "q-135486" :question/problem "Which of the following are stochastic matrices?\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}0.1 & 0.7 \\\\ 0.9 & 0.3\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}0.45 & 0.35 \\\\ 0.25 & 0.65\\end{aligned}],\\,W=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a stochastic vector is a vector with nonnegative entries that add up to $1.$ A matrix is stochastic if all its columns are stochastic vectors.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices in turn.\n\n- Matrix $U$ is a stochastic matrix. Indeed, each column is a stochastic vector (the corresponding entries are nonnegative and add up to one): \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}0.1 & 0.7 \\\\ 0.9 & 0.3\\end{aligned}]\\,\\begin{aligned}0.1+0.9=1 \\\\ 0.7+0.3=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Matrix $V$ is *not* a stochastic matrix since its first column is not a stochastic vector (the corresponding entries don't add up to one): \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0.45 & 0.35 \\\\ 0.25 & 0.65\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Matrix $W$  *not* a stochastic matrix since its second column is not a stochastic vector (it contains negative entries):\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$U$ only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9b9b2d59-8140-5362-8fc0-b70ab471b530"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9b9b2d59-8140-5362-8fc0-b70ab471b530" :answer-field/id #uuid "9b9b2d59-8140-5362-8fc0-b70ab471b530" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9748d7be-c943-5b7a-8ed6-ed3b73afb63f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4216f855-abd4-509e-b9fe-1f121e941dc6" "answer-76d69def-a627-5cf5-94e5-9d688f380f9c" "answer-9748d7be-c943-5b7a-8ed6-ed3b73afb63f" "answer-7140a834-dbc4-5e37-81b0-24348554cc3b" "answer-634b88fd-fbd1-55cf-a285-25f45e9c0447"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4216f855-abd4-509e-b9fe-1f121e941dc6" :answer/id #uuid "4216f855-abd4-509e-b9fe-1f121e941dc6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U$ and $V$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-76d69def-a627-5cf5-94e5-9d688f380f9c" :answer/id #uuid "76d69def-a627-5cf5-94e5-9d688f380f9c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U$ and $W$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9748d7be-c943-5b7a-8ed6-ed3b73afb63f" :answer/id #uuid "9748d7be-c943-5b7a-8ed6-ed3b73afb63f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7140a834-dbc4-5e37-81b0-24348554cc3b" :answer/id #uuid "7140a834-dbc4-5e37-81b0-24348554cc3b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U,$ $V,$ and $W$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-634b88fd-fbd1-55cf-a285-25f45e9c0447" :answer/id #uuid "634b88fd-fbd1-55cf-a285-25f45e9c0447" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$V$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-55574236-41f2-5d82-abc0-f140064784e6" :question/id #uuid "55574236-41f2-5d82-abc0-f140064784e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-135481" :question/problem "Which of the following are stochastic vectors?\n\n$$\nu=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0.5\\end{aligned}],\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}-0.5 \\\\ 1.5\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0.1 \\\\ 0.9\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a stochastic vector is a vector with nonnegative entries that add up to $1.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our vectors in turn.\n\n- Vector $u$ is *not*  a stochastic vector since the entries do not add up to one:\n\n$$\n0+0.5=0.5\\ne 1\n$$\n\n- Vector $v$ is *not* a stochastic vector since it contains negative entries.\n\n- Vector $w$ is a stochastic vector. Indeed, \n\n- its entries are all nonnegative, and\n\n- the entries add up to one:\n\n$$\n0+0.1+0.9=1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$w$ only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8c8d9e16-689e-57a7-9c40-a1537c1647fb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8c8d9e16-689e-57a7-9c40-a1537c1647fb" :answer-field/id #uuid "8c8d9e16-689e-57a7-9c40-a1537c1647fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5566d9eb-9357-5cab-bfb4-b03789725566" :answer-field/choices ["answer-01856f5b-cc6c-5c01-87c6-35513dae3331" "answer-ae7e88a2-b349-5d40-9e95-5904b7a47fe6" "answer-5092eb4e-8f98-579e-b1a4-2b0ec10dcf24" "answer-ce51276c-e4d8-5e7f-ad9a-e2ef4556a160" "answer-5566d9eb-9357-5cab-bfb4-b03789725566"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01856f5b-cc6c-5c01-87c6-35513dae3331" :answer/id #uuid "01856f5b-cc6c-5c01-87c6-35513dae3331" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$u$ and $w$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae7e88a2-b349-5d40-9e95-5904b7a47fe6" :answer/id #uuid "ae7e88a2-b349-5d40-9e95-5904b7a47fe6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$u$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5092eb4e-8f98-579e-b1a4-2b0ec10dcf24" :answer/id #uuid "5092eb4e-8f98-579e-b1a4-2b0ec10dcf24" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$u,$ $v,$ and $w$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce51276c-e4d8-5e7f-ad9a-e2ef4556a160" :answer/id #uuid "ce51276c-e4d8-5e7f-ad9a-e2ef4556a160" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$v$ and $w$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5566d9eb-9357-5cab-bfb4-b03789725566" :answer/id #uuid "5566d9eb-9357-5cab-bfb4-b03789725566" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$w$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124769 :question/problem "Which of the following are stochastic matrices?\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}0.2 & 0 \\\\ 0.5 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}0.45 & 0.25 \\\\ 0.55 & 0.75\\end{aligned}],\\,W=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0.5 & 0.2 & 0.3 \\\\ 0.5 & 0 & 0.7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a stochastic vector is a vector with nonnegative entries that add up to $1.$ A matrix is stochastic if all its columns are stochastic vectors.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices in turn.\n\n- Matrix $U$ is *not* a stochastic matrix since its first column is not a stochastic vector (the corresponding entries don't add up to one): \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0.2 & 0 \\\\ 0.5 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Matrix $V$ is a stochastic matrix. Indeed, each column is a stochastic vector (the corresponding entries are nonnegative and add up to one): \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}0.45 & 0.25 \\\\ 0.55 & 0.75\\end{aligned}]\\,\\begin{aligned}0.45+0.55=1 \\\\ 0.25+0.75=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Matrix $W$ is *not* a stochastic matrix since its second column is not a stochastic vector (the corresponding entries don't add up to one): \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0.5 & 0.2 & 0.3 \\\\ 0.5 & 0 & 0.7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$V$ only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121211 :answer-field/correct 17592186121213 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-7d2bfda5-1f22-5eca-90c5-42502b97859c" :question/id #uuid "7d2bfda5-1f22-5eca-90c5-42502b97859c" :question/math-academy-id "q-135564" :question/problem "There are three supermarket chains in a particular city: chain $A,$ chain $B,$ and chain $C.$ A study has shown that, each month\n\n- from the customers that prefer chain $A,$ $5%$ change to chain $B$ and $15%$ change to chain $C,$\n\n- from the customers that prefer chain $B,$ $25%$ change to chain $A$ and $25%$ change to chain $C,$\n\n- from the customers that prefer chain $C,$ $15%$ change to chain $A$ and $35%$ change to chain $B.$\n\nThe stochastic matrix that describes this situation is given below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.8 & a & 0.15 \\\\ b & 0.5 & 0.35 \\\\ 0.15 & 0.25 & c\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the following situation for each month:\n\n- From the customers that prefer chain $A,$ $5%$ change to chain $B$ and $15%$ change to chain $C.$ This implies that $80%$ of them continue to prefer chain $A.$\n\n- From the customers that prefer chain $B,$ $25%$ change to chain $A$ and $25%$ change to chain $C.$ This implies that $50%$ of them continue to prefer chain $B.$\n\n- From the customers that prefer chain $C,$ $15%$ change to chain $A$ and $35%$ change to chain $B.$ This implies that $50%$ of them continue to prefer chain $C.$\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\">From:</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Chain A</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Chain B</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Chain C</b></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"3\">To:</td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Chain A</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.15$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Chain B</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.05$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.5$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.35$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Chain C</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.15$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.5$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nWe can write the corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.8 & 0.25 & 0.15 \\\\ 0.05 & 0.5 & 0.35 \\\\ 0.15 & 0.25 & 0.5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=0.25+0.05+0.5=0.8.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-87636227-a251-5be3-befa-08c44f225fa6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-87636227-a251-5be3-befa-08c44f225fa6" :answer-field/id #uuid "87636227-a251-5be3-befa-08c44f225fa6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b7b44784-1307-5ab1-8d5a-2ec2e4bf1930" :answer-field/choices ["answer-77d648dd-908d-5044-81c9-f4c8de288371" "answer-b7b44784-1307-5ab1-8d5a-2ec2e4bf1930" "answer-277522b5-e3dd-5b89-81f3-5cdba4469a16" "answer-98ceb55d-c397-5695-99ff-7995f7e2e05a" "answer-b6eebac0-9289-5154-9d7a-80de8f6fa66c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-77d648dd-908d-5044-81c9-f4c8de288371" :answer/id #uuid "77d648dd-908d-5044-81c9-f4c8de288371" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b7b44784-1307-5ab1-8d5a-2ec2e4bf1930" :answer/id #uuid "b7b44784-1307-5ab1-8d5a-2ec2e4bf1930" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-277522b5-e3dd-5b89-81f3-5cdba4469a16" :answer/id #uuid "277522b5-e3dd-5b89-81f3-5cdba4469a16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-98ceb55d-c397-5695-99ff-7995f7e2e05a" :answer/id #uuid "98ceb55d-c397-5695-99ff-7995f7e2e05a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.95" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b6eebac0-9289-5154-9d7a-80de8f6fa66c" :answer/id #uuid "b6eebac0-9289-5154-9d7a-80de8f6fa66c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124913 :question/problem "There are three groups of fans in a certain town: those who prefer basketball, those who prefer baseball, and those who prefer football. A study has shown that, each year\n\n- from the people that prefer basketball, $32%$ change to baseball and $28%$ change to football,\n\n- from the people that prefer baseball, $45%$ change to football and $15%$ change to basketball,\n\n- from the people that prefer football, $25%$ change to basketball and $65%$ change to baseball.\n\nThe stochastic matrix that describes this situation is given below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.4 & 0.15 & a \\\\ 0.32 & b & 0.65 \\\\ c & 0.45 & 0.1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the following situation for each year:\n\n- From the people who prefer basketball, $32%$ change to baseball and $28%$ change to football. This implies that $40%$ of them continue to prefer basketball.\n\n- From people who prefer baseball, $45%$ change to football and $15%$ change to basketball. This implies that $40%$ of them continue to prefer baseball.\n\n- From people who prefer football, $25%$ change to basketball and $65%$ change to baseball. This implies that $10%$ of them continue to prefer football.\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\">From:</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Basketball</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Baseball</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Football</b></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"3\">To:</td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Basketball</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.15$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Baseball</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.32$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.65$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Football</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.28$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.45$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.1$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nWe can write the corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.4 & 0.15 & 0.25 \\\\ 0.32 & 0.4 & 0.65 \\\\ 0.28 & 0.45 & 0.1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=0.25+0.4+0.28=0.93.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186122078 :answer-field/correct 17592186122082 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-1cf7f6b8-f438-52c0-a338-61f2ad7fa03e" :question/id #uuid "1cf7f6b8-f438-52c0-a338-61f2ad7fa03e" :question/math-academy-id "q-135555" :question/problem "In a particular country, there are two groups of people: those who live in the cities and those who live in the countryside. A study has shown that each decade \n\n- $12%$ of people who lived in the cities relocate to the countryside, and\n\n- $28%$ of people who lived in the countryside relocate to the cities.\n\nWhich of the following tables describes how these people change their preferences each year?" :question/worked-solution "We are given the following situation for each decade: \n\n- $12%$ of people who live in the cities relocate to the countryside. This implies that $88%$ of them remain living in the cities.\n\n- $28%$ of people who live in the countryside relocate to the cities. This implies that $72%$ of them remain living in the countryside.\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"2\">From:</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"60\"><b>Cities</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"60\"><b>Countryside</b></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">To:</td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"60\"><b>Cities</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.88$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.28$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"60\"><b>Countryside</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.12$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.72$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nNote that we can write a corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0.88 & 0.28 \\\\ 0.12 & 0.72\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6f6518b4-e34a-514d-90e9-c9eb50aaae11"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6f6518b4-e34a-514d-90e9-c9eb50aaae11" :answer-field/id #uuid "6f6518b4-e34a-514d-90e9-c9eb50aaae11" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ae851e7a-57eb-52b1-8b52-dcf69a01f009" :answer-field/choices ["ans